WEBVTT

1
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.085
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHIRPING]</font></b>

2
00:01:01.135 --> 00:01:02.595
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Once upon a time,

3
00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:06.558
there was a magical place
called the Motherland,

4
00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:10.270
where Fairy Godmothers lived and learned

5
00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:13.147
all they needed to know
about godmothering.

6
00:01:13.231 --> 00:01:14.899
Oh, blah, blah, blah.

7
00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:17.151
We all know how this bit goes.

8
00:01:17.235 --> 00:01:19.362
This is not your usual fairy tale.

9
00:01:19.696 --> 00:01:22.699
Fairy tales end with "happily ever after,"

10
00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.826
and that's where we begin.

11
00:01:25.326 --> 00:01:29.247
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Good morning, Motherland!

12
00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:33.835
It's almost the weekend,
and you know what that means.

13
00:01:34.377 --> 00:01:40.008
Grab a pumpkin, raise your wands,
break out the glass slippers,

14
00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:43.803
it's time to party like it's 1699.

15
00:01:43.887 --> 00:01:47.765
I'm gonna kick things off
with everyone's favorite pop hit.

16
00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:52.061
<b><font color="#ca004b">[OPERA MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

17
00:01:54.606 --> 00:01:59.277
I'm Agnes.
I'm 172 years old at least.

18
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.738
And I'm too cool for school.

19
00:02:02.071 --> 00:02:06.826
It's why they made me the resident DJ,
and I don't have to go to lessons.

20
00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.246
But this isn't about me.

21
00:02:10.622 --> 00:02:12.540
This is the story of Eleanor.

22
00:02:13.374 --> 00:02:16.169
She's the Motherland's youngest trainee

23
00:02:16.252 --> 00:02:20.173
and the only person
who's bothered to apply in decades.

24
00:02:21.424 --> 00:02:23.676
All she wanted was to graduate,

25
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.762
to be a real Fairy Godmother,

26
00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:29.265
to have her name in a book
alongside the greats.

27
00:02:29.891 --> 00:02:32.894
That's her in the pink, without any pals.

28
00:02:32.977 --> 00:02:34.217
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHATTER]</font></b>

29
00:02:36.731 --> 00:02:38.491
- Uh-oh, here comes trouble.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[DOOR OPENING]</font></b>

30
00:02:39.108 --> 00:02:42.070
This is Moira, the headmistress.

31
00:02:42.153 --> 00:02:45.823
She wrote the book
on Fairy Godmothering, literally.

32
00:02:45.907 --> 00:02:48.409
Let us open our texts, shall we?

33
00:02:49.619 --> 00:02:54.165
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> She's been banging on
about the same old formula for centuries.

34
00:02:54.249 --> 00:02:56.835
Yesterday, we reviewed step one.

35
00:02:56.918 --> 00:02:59.087
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Oh, you didn't know
there was a formula?

36
00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:00.547
Recite it with me, please.

37
00:03:01.172 --> 00:03:05.844
<b><font color="#cf685c">ALL:</font></b> A glittery gown
turns a frown upside down.

38
00:03:14.143 --> 00:03:16.938
Ooh! Oh, wow!

39
00:03:18.606 --> 00:03:20.817
- Ooh!
- It's just the same.

40
00:03:21.442 --> 00:03:24.946
Once you've conjured the gown,
you're on your way to step two.

41
00:03:25.029 --> 00:03:28.741
- Which is?
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ALL:</font></b> Find their true love.

42
00:03:28.825 --> 00:03:30.368
Correct.

43
00:03:30.451 --> 00:03:33.580
Now, once the gown and true love
are in place,

44
00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:36.374
we move on to step three.

45
00:03:36.457 --> 00:03:37.834
Which is?

46
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.544
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Oh, please?
- Anyone?

47
00:03:39.669 --> 00:03:42.005
- Anybody?
- Oh, I know it.

48
00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.798
- You?
- My arm's tired.

49
00:03:43.882 --> 00:03:45.442
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MOIRA:</font></b> Anyone else?
- Hurts to hold it up.

50
00:03:45.466 --> 00:03:46.467
Literally anyone.

51
00:03:46.551 --> 00:03:48.887
- Oh. Oh, please?
- Yes.

52
00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:51.931
- Happily ever after.
- Correct.

53
00:03:52.015 --> 00:03:53.183
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>

54
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.519
Really?
Again with the formula?

55
00:03:57.187 --> 00:03:59.814
- Can we do something different today?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

56
00:03:59.898 --> 00:04:04.152
<b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b> No.
Because we never really do anything.

57
00:04:04.235 --> 00:04:06.070
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL CHUCKLE]</font></b>

58
00:04:06.154 --> 00:04:07.530
Enough!

59
00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.157
Enough!

60
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.743
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> And this is where
the problems really started,

61
00:04:11.826 --> 00:04:15.413
because Moira is not
someone you want to cross.

62
00:04:15.497 --> 00:04:19.834
Step three is happily ever after.

63
00:04:20.502 --> 00:04:23.546
- It just happens.
- Yes, it just happens.

64
00:04:24.422 --> 00:04:25.548
It's step three.

65
00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.301
If you're confused,
I can be your study buddy.

66
00:04:28.843 --> 00:04:31.346
I'm totally available,
like, anytime, day or night.

67
00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.182
<b><font color="#cf685c">MOIRA:</font></b> There's no reason to be confused.

68
00:04:34.265 --> 00:04:39.979
The formula has been the cornerstone
of Fairy Godmothering since it began

69
00:04:40.063 --> 00:04:42.815
because it works.

70
00:04:42.899 --> 00:04:44.526
If it works,

71
00:04:44.943 --> 00:04:47.362
then why is everything around here
falling apart?

72
00:04:47.445 --> 00:04:48.446
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL GASP]</font></b>

73
00:04:48.696 --> 00:04:52.867
Everyone knows that people have
stopped believing in happily ever after.

74
00:04:55.912 --> 00:04:57.872
Well, everyone except Eleanor, that is.

75
00:04:57.956 --> 00:05:00.834
And she's never gonna be
a Fairy Godmother.

76
00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:02.585
Well, you said so yourself.

77
00:05:04.963 --> 00:05:07.090
When's the last time
anyone went on assignment?

78
00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.925
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL MURMURING]</font></b>

79
00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.721
No more assignments
mean no more Fairy Godmothers.

80
00:05:13.805 --> 00:05:18.184
So when exactly were you going to
fess up to her and us

81
00:05:18.268 --> 00:05:20.854
that you are about to
shut this school down,

82
00:05:20.937 --> 00:05:24.065
and we are all being retrained
as Tooth Fairies?

83
00:05:24.148 --> 00:05:25.149
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

84
00:05:25.233 --> 00:05:27.610
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
What?

85
00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:30.280
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> And this was the moment
that Eleanor realized

86
00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:35.034
she would never be a Fairy Godmother
unless she found an assignment.

87
00:05:36.744 --> 00:05:40.540
Now, being a Tooth Fairy
didn't sound so bad to me.

88
00:05:40.665 --> 00:05:42.000
You only work nights,

89
00:05:42.083 --> 00:05:44.669
you've always got
a little change in your pocket.

90
00:05:45.295 --> 00:05:49.424
But Eleanor, she was
not about to give up her dream.

91
00:05:49.507 --> 00:05:52.719
All she needed was one assignment.

92
00:05:53.636 --> 00:05:56.931
And about 40 to 50 years more training.

93
00:05:57.515 --> 00:05:59.475
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Whoa! Ouch!

94
00:06:00.518 --> 00:06:03.313
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>
Ow. Oof!

95
00:06:03.897 --> 00:06:05.815
There has to be something in here.

96
00:06:06.274 --> 00:06:08.985
Wish I could levitate.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

97
00:06:09.903 --> 00:06:11.654
Nothing. Nothing.

98
00:06:11.905 --> 00:06:13.823
Nothing! Ugh! Nothing?

99
00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:16.075
Nothing!

100
00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:18.119
Okay. I give up.

101
00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:21.706
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> And just when
she thought all was lost...

102
00:06:23.374 --> 00:06:25.168
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Wait. What?

103
00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.252
Please.

104
00:06:28.421 --> 00:06:29.589
Yes!

105
00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:33.635
<b><font color="#cf685c">YOUNG MACKENZIE:</font></b> Dear Fairy Godmother,
my name is Mackenzie Walsh,

106
00:06:33.718 --> 00:06:38.223
and I live at 8566 Hawkins Street
in Boston. In America.

107
00:06:38.515 --> 00:06:39.724
And I need your help.

108
00:06:40.517 --> 00:06:41.809
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR SCREAMS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[THUD]</font></b>

109
00:06:41.893 --> 00:06:43.353
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b>
I'm okay.

110
00:07:01.871 --> 00:07:04.749
<b><font color="#cf685c">YOUNG MACKENZIE:</font></b> Obviously I would like world peace,

111
00:07:04.833 --> 00:07:07.836
but there is also a boy in my class,

112
00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:11.214
and he is the cutest boy
in the whole school.

113
00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:14.175
It is my dearest wish
that he would even notice me.

114
00:07:14.259 --> 00:07:17.053
Please, could you help
make that wish come true?

115
00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.471
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Toothbrush.

116
00:07:20.265 --> 00:07:22.433
Nightgown. Books:

117
00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:25.520
- Howdy!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[YELPS]</font></b>

118
00:07:26.104 --> 00:07:27.397
Where are you going?

119
00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.941
What?
No, I'm not going anywhere.

120
00:07:30.024 --> 00:07:33.778
If I was going somewhere,
I'd be packing away my books. Like this.

121
00:07:33.862 --> 00:07:35.238
And my toothbrush.

122
00:07:36.239 --> 00:07:39.659
And my extra underpants.
Like this.

123
00:07:39.742 --> 00:07:41.995
Oh, and my spare wand.
In case of emergencies.

124
00:07:42.078 --> 00:07:44.914
Did you see me do that?
No. I don't think so.

125
00:07:44.998 --> 00:07:49.002
I know what you're doing, Eleanor,
I just don't know why.

126
00:07:52.797 --> 00:07:56.134
- Can you keep a secret?
- I am a secret.

127
00:07:56.217 --> 00:07:57.552
I went to the Assignment Room.

128
00:07:57.635 --> 00:08:01.764
Why? It's empty.
That's why they're shutting us down.

129
00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:04.893
It's not totally empty.
I found an assignment.

130
00:08:04.976 --> 00:08:06.936
- Get outta here!
- No.

131
00:08:08.271 --> 00:08:09.272
Look.

132
00:08:10.982 --> 00:08:13.359
Mackenzie Walsh, age ten.

133
00:08:13.443 --> 00:08:15.904
I'm gonna help that little girl
and save the Motherland

134
00:08:15.987 --> 00:08:19.699
by proving that
people still need Fairy Godmothers.

135
00:08:19.782 --> 00:08:21.743
Well, you got moxie, kiddo.

136
00:08:22.494 --> 00:08:25.330
But even if this girl
does need a Fairy Godmother,

137
00:08:25.413 --> 00:08:26.873
you're not trained.

138
00:08:26.956 --> 00:08:30.126
Well, I'm not going to get trained
if the Motherland is shut down.

139
00:08:30.210 --> 00:08:34.589
And even if I don't know everything,
I know that I can do this.

140
00:08:35.965 --> 00:08:41.095
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING]</font></b>
I was born to be a Fairy Godmother

141
00:08:41.179 --> 00:08:43.932
It's in the very heart of me

142
00:08:44.474 --> 00:08:45.475
Ow!

143
00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:48.770
You know you're not supposed to sing.
We've talked about it.

144
00:08:48.853 --> 00:08:51.147
You're gonna miss my singing
when I'm gone.

145
00:08:51.231 --> 00:08:52.649
Trust me when I tell you

146
00:08:52.732 --> 00:08:55.276
there are worse things
than being a Tooth Fairy.

147
00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:58.696
Moira's not a big fan
of fairies going rogue.

148
00:08:58.988 --> 00:09:03.535
If she finds out you're gone,
she could close the portals back,

149
00:09:03.618 --> 00:09:05.370
or take away your magic.

150
00:09:05.453 --> 00:09:07.705
Shh, don't say that.

151
00:09:08.998 --> 00:09:10.250
I have to do this.

152
00:09:10.708 --> 00:09:15.421
Well, if you're going, you're gonna
need to know the way out of here.

153
00:09:25.473 --> 00:09:27.100
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BLOWS NOSE]</font></b>

154
00:09:30.854 --> 00:09:31.855
Right.

155
00:09:36.818 --> 00:09:38.653
- Kid, you'd better move fast.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

156
00:09:38.736 --> 00:09:43.032
You only have a few more days
before Moira closes us down.

157
00:09:44.284 --> 00:09:45.535
Thank you, Agnes.

158
00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:47.328
Knock 'em dead, kid.

159
00:09:47.412 --> 00:09:51.457
Oh, Agnes, if everything goes right,
nobody's gonna die.

160
00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:54.127
Goodbye.

161
00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.211
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BIRDS CHIRPING]</font></b>

162
00:10:08.224 --> 00:10:09.350
Oh.

163
00:10:14.564 --> 00:10:17.442
I can do this, I can do this.

164
00:10:17.525 --> 00:10:18.526
I can do this.

165
00:10:22.447 --> 00:10:24.157
I can't do this.

166
00:10:24.866 --> 00:10:25.867
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

167
00:10:43.009 --> 00:10:44.010
Oh.

168
00:10:44.511 --> 00:10:46.346
Nicely done.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

169
00:10:50.308 --> 00:10:51.309
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTING]</font></b>

170
00:11:00.109 --> 00:11:01.402
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SQUEALS]</font></b>

171
00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:02.695
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[THUD]</font></b>

172
00:11:02.779 --> 00:11:04.364
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b>

173
00:11:06.074 --> 00:11:07.075
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BREATHING HEAVILY]</font></b>

174
00:11:20.755 --> 00:11:21.756
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

175
00:11:36.104 --> 00:11:37.564
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMING]</font></b>

176
00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:53.371
And they say portal crossing
is a senior-level course. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

177
00:11:54.497 --> 00:11:57.250
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
What in Godmother's name!

178
00:12:04.299 --> 00:12:07.802
Hello, friends.
Which way to America?

179
00:12:07.886 --> 00:12:10.555
East? West? Oh, both.

180
00:12:11.097 --> 00:12:12.265
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

181
00:12:12.348 --> 00:12:14.142
Pumpkins! Yes!

182
00:12:16.019 --> 00:12:17.061
All right.

183
00:12:19.105 --> 00:12:20.773
One carriage, coming up.

184
00:12:20.857 --> 00:12:21.858
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

185
00:12:26.196 --> 00:12:27.197
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

186
00:12:28.031 --> 00:12:29.032
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

187
00:12:32.619 --> 00:12:33.703
<b><font color="#ca004b">[EXCLAIMING]</font></b>

188
00:12:35.997 --> 00:12:37.165
Oh, no!

189
00:12:38.583 --> 00:12:39.584
Not the big one!

190
00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.841
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>

191
00:12:48.218 --> 00:12:50.303
There's gotta be a better way to travel.

192
00:12:51.721 --> 00:12:53.181
<b><font color="#ca004b">[COUNTRY MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

193
00:12:53.264 --> 00:12:54.766
<b><font color="#ca004b">[PANTING]</font></b>

194
00:13:02.899 --> 00:13:03.900
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CAR HONKS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>

195
00:13:24.295 --> 00:13:26.464
Hey. Hey!

196
00:13:27.632 --> 00:13:28.675
Hey, are you okay?

197
00:13:28.758 --> 00:13:29.759
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BOTH SCREAM]</font></b>

198
00:13:30.802 --> 00:13:32.262
You can't sleep here.

199
00:13:32.762 --> 00:13:36.224
- Why? Are there dragons? Evil fairies?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>

200
00:13:36.307 --> 00:13:37.976
In a manner of speaking, yeah.

201
00:13:38.059 --> 00:13:39.060
Oh.

202
00:13:39.644 --> 00:13:40.770
Whoa!

203
00:13:40.854 --> 00:13:44.274
Oh, your carriage must've required
an enormous pumpkin.

204
00:13:44.357 --> 00:13:46.025
How many footmen are inside?

205
00:13:46.109 --> 00:13:48.778
Uh, none. Just me.

206
00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:50.363
Beth.

207
00:13:50.446 --> 00:13:51.447
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

208
00:13:53.867 --> 00:13:56.870
Beth. You're hilarious.

209
00:13:56.953 --> 00:13:59.205
Everyone knows
women don't drive themselves.

210
00:13:59.289 --> 00:14:00.874
That's what mice are for.

211
00:14:01.916 --> 00:14:04.586
- Sweetheart, are you on drugs?
- Of course not.

212
00:14:06.129 --> 00:14:07.130
What are drugs?

213
00:14:07.714 --> 00:14:09.174
Oh, boy, that's a yes.

214
00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.010
Look, do you have anyone you can call?

215
00:14:12.093 --> 00:14:13.845
I guess there's my roommate.

216
00:14:13.928 --> 00:14:15.180
<b><font color="#ca004b">[LOUDLY]</font></b>
Agnes!

217
00:14:15.847 --> 00:14:18.474
Agnes! Agnes?

218
00:14:19.976 --> 00:14:22.228
She must be doing
her morning announcements.

219
00:14:22.312 --> 00:14:24.522
I can find a bluebird
to bring her a message

220
00:14:24.606 --> 00:14:25.607
once I get to Boston.

221
00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.233
Is that where you're headed?

222
00:14:27.317 --> 00:14:31.029
Oh, yes. I'm looking for
my future forever friend, Mackenzie Walsh.

223
00:14:31.487 --> 00:14:36.284
She lives in Boston, Massachusetts.
In America.

224
00:14:36.367 --> 00:14:38.286
Let's see what we can find.

225
00:14:38.369 --> 00:14:39.704
Oh, good, a map.

226
00:14:40.413 --> 00:14:42.999
Siri, search Mackenzie Walsh.

227
00:14:43.208 --> 00:14:45.752
<b><font color="#ca004b">[AUTOMATED VOICE OVER SPEAKER]</font></b>
Okay. Here's what I found.

228
00:14:45.835 --> 00:14:48.213
Who said that?
Is there a genie in there?

229
00:14:48.296 --> 00:14:49.589
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SOFTLY]</font></b>
Don't answer that.

230
00:14:49.964 --> 00:14:53.051
Okay. I think we need to
get you to your friend

231
00:14:53.134 --> 00:14:55.053
- as quickly as possible.
- Yes.

232
00:14:55.136 --> 00:14:57.889
- The good news is, I'm headed that way.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>

233
00:14:59.599 --> 00:15:00.600
Okay.

234
00:15:01.309 --> 00:15:02.310
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR GRUNTS]</font></b>

235
00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:22.580
<b><font color="#cf685c">BETH:</font></b> Welcome to Beantown.

236
00:15:24.374 --> 00:15:26.835
So then I said,
"I don't want to be a Tooth Fairy."

237
00:15:26.918 --> 00:15:30.839
Yep. I lost my heart to a Tooth Fairy
one night at Burning Man in 2004.

238
00:15:30.922 --> 00:15:32.257
They're no good.

239
00:15:33.007 --> 00:15:36.469
Well, you should be able to find
a Mackenzie Walsh in there.

240
00:15:36.553 --> 00:15:39.514
- Oh, thank you for everything.
- Oh. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

241
00:15:43.226 --> 00:15:45.103
Hey, take this.

242
00:15:45.186 --> 00:15:46.187
Thank you.

243
00:15:46.479 --> 00:15:49.190
Are you sure I can't
make you a ball gown before I go?

244
00:15:49.274 --> 00:15:51.776
Nah. I got a few in the back.

245
00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.111
Oh, thank goodness.

246
00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:54.821
Bye.

247
00:15:54.904 --> 00:15:55.989
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

248
00:15:56.072 --> 00:15:57.448
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHATTER]</font></b>

249
00:15:58.867 --> 00:15:59.868
Ooh.

250
00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:08.751
<b><font color="#cf685c">BARB:</font></b> Coming up...

251
00:16:08.835 --> 00:16:10.545
What would you do if you found out

252
00:16:10.628 --> 00:16:13.673
your parents weren't actually
your parents at all?

253
00:16:13.756 --> 00:16:18.136
That's the dilemma faced by two men,
both born in the Massachusetts area.

254
00:16:18.219 --> 00:16:21.055
The babies were switched at birth
and reunited with their families

255
00:16:21.139 --> 00:16:22.515
20 years later,

256
00:16:22.599 --> 00:16:26.186
only to discover that the hospital
had it right the first time.

257
00:16:26.269 --> 00:16:30.148
But our top story tonight
is out of Essex County,

258
00:16:30.231 --> 00:16:33.610
where residents
were left shocked and confused.

259
00:16:33.693 --> 00:16:37.071
Look at this barbaric sight.

260
00:16:37.614 --> 00:16:40.742
- Now, police have no motives...
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

261
00:16:40.825 --> 00:16:42.994
...for the destruction
of the pumpkin patch,

262
00:16:43.077 --> 00:16:46.039
but believe local pranksters
may be to blame.

263
00:16:46.122 --> 00:16:49.417
If only these inflatable scarecrows
could talk.

264
00:16:49.501 --> 00:16:50.877
Back to you, Barb.

265
00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:54.714
Thanks, Hugh, for that explosive update.

266
00:16:54.797 --> 00:16:56.007
We'll be back in a minute

267
00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:58.760
with news of a bed
that was delivered up a ladder

268
00:16:58.843 --> 00:17:00.053
in Dedham yesterday.

269
00:17:00.512 --> 00:17:02.263
Please text or tweet us

270
00:17:02.347 --> 00:17:05.934
the strangest things
you've seen going up a ladder.

271
00:17:06.017 --> 00:17:07.578
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[BELL RINGS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">WOMAN:</font></b> You can't be here!

272
00:17:07.602 --> 00:17:08.842
<b><font color="#ca004b">[LOUDLY]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">GRANT:</font></b> Really, people?

273
00:17:10.813 --> 00:17:12.440
That's the best you got?

274
00:17:13.399 --> 00:17:14.651
Conference room!

275
00:17:15.693 --> 00:17:16.694
Now!

276
00:17:17.028 --> 00:17:18.655
<b><font color="#cf685c">WOMAN:</font></b> What do you think you're doing?

277
00:17:18.738 --> 00:17:21.991
Looking for a sad little girl
named Mackenzie Walsh.

278
00:17:22.075 --> 00:17:25.703
Awkward haircut,
red, like an angry leprechaun.

279
00:17:26.454 --> 00:17:30.750
Kelly in Brookline has emailed.
She once saw a duck on a ladder.

280
00:17:30.834 --> 00:17:33.044
So deal with that bombshell
how you see fit.

281
00:17:33.127 --> 00:17:34.879
Mack, you have a visitor.

282
00:17:34.963 --> 00:17:35.964
Uh-huh.

283
00:17:36.506 --> 00:17:38.132
I'm looking for Mackenzie Walsh.

284
00:17:38.216 --> 00:17:39.509
Yep, that is me.

285
00:17:40.385 --> 00:17:42.595
Hey, Murry, can you please move it along?

286
00:17:42.679 --> 00:17:44.514
I promised my kids
I'd cook dinner tonight.

287
00:17:44.639 --> 00:17:48.017
Then I must be looking for your daughter.
Could you tell me how to find her?

288
00:17:49.602 --> 00:17:52.272
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCOFFS]</font></b> Who are you?
The world's laziest kidnapper?

289
00:17:53.064 --> 00:17:54.941
Why would I tell you where my kid is?

290
00:17:55.024 --> 00:17:56.818
Is this someone's idea of a joke?

291
00:17:58.361 --> 00:18:00.905
I'm sorry, I think
there must be some mistake.

292
00:18:00.989 --> 00:18:04.951
I'm looking for the Mackenzie Walsh
that lives at 8566 Hawkins Street.

293
00:18:06.703 --> 00:18:08.288
How do you know my old address?

294
00:18:08.872 --> 00:18:09.873
Your old...

295
00:18:11.249 --> 00:18:12.250
No.

296
00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.419
No, no, no.

297
00:18:14.502 --> 00:18:16.212
No, it can't be you. You're...

298
00:18:16.296 --> 00:18:18.298
Old. So old.

299
00:18:18.381 --> 00:18:21.801
This is a disaster.
A woman your age couldn't possibly

300
00:18:21.885 --> 00:18:23.970
still need someone
to make her dreams come true.

301
00:18:24.053 --> 00:18:26.139
Yeah, right,
because I'm clearly living the dream.

302
00:18:26.222 --> 00:18:27.223
Now, who are you?

303
00:18:27.891 --> 00:18:29.225
Well, I'm Eleanor,

304
00:18:29.309 --> 00:18:31.561
- and I'm your Fairy Godmother.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SOFTLY]</font></b> Security.

305
00:18:31.644 --> 00:18:34.439
And I'm here to help you
find happily ever after.

306
00:18:34.522 --> 00:18:36.107
Oh, you wanna be on the show. Okay.

307
00:18:36.191 --> 00:18:39.402
Uh, are you from a matchmaking app,
a dating website, what?

308
00:18:39.485 --> 00:18:41.571
Oh, actually, I'm from the Motherland.

309
00:18:41.654 --> 00:18:43.573
Right. I've never heard of that.

310
00:18:43.656 --> 00:18:45.016
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SOFTLY]</font></b> Security.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">WOMAN:</font></b> Mack.

311
00:18:45.492 --> 00:18:47.368
Grant says get in here. Now.

312
00:18:47.452 --> 00:18:49.496
- I'm late for a story meeting.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Oh.

313
00:18:49.579 --> 00:18:51.265
Come up with something
a little more original

314
00:18:51.289 --> 00:18:52.665
than the Fairy Godmother act,

315
00:18:52.749 --> 00:18:55.293
and maybe we can get you
a segment for Valentine's Day.

316
00:18:55.376 --> 00:18:57.056
- It's not an act. I really...
- Over here.

317
00:18:57.545 --> 00:18:58.963
- Ma'am.
- Oh, footmen?

318
00:18:59.255 --> 00:19:02.884
<b><font color="#cf685c">GRANT:</font></b> Okay. The viewing numbers are in,
folks, and they are not a pretty read.

319
00:19:02.967 --> 00:19:05.261
I mean, look at this. We're still in...
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SMACKS LIPS]</font></b>

320
00:19:05.345 --> 00:19:07.263
- I don't know how to read this.
- Fifth place.

321
00:19:07.347 --> 00:19:10.433
Fifth, like five?
There are only four news shows.

322
00:19:10.517 --> 00:19:13.603
Okay, I could try
a different shade of spray tan.

323
00:19:13.686 --> 00:19:15.980
No, no, ever since we switched you
to coconut glow,

324
00:19:16.064 --> 00:19:18.149
you are killing it
with teen girls and shut-ins.

325
00:19:18.233 --> 00:19:20.818
It's the rest of you
that need to step your game up.

326
00:19:20.902 --> 00:19:22.403
Especially you two!

327
00:19:22.487 --> 00:19:23.780
What was that?

328
00:19:24.155 --> 00:19:26.699
"Cops think
pranksters blew up some pumpkins."

329
00:19:26.783 --> 00:19:28.868
That is not getting eyes on the box.

330
00:19:28.952 --> 00:19:35.458
But, "Police rule out witchcraft
in mysterious pumpkin cult massacre"?

331
00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.085
That's a story!

332
00:19:37.168 --> 00:19:39.838
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> I really am her Fairy Godmother.

333
00:19:39.921 --> 00:19:41.756
Do you wanna see my magic wand?

334
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.466
I mean, look what Dave did last month.

335
00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:46.177
Dave forgot to bring us back
from commercial for 12 minutes,

336
00:19:46.261 --> 00:19:47.387
and nobody noticed.

337
00:19:48.054 --> 00:19:51.224
Wrong.
Dave got people talking about us.

338
00:19:51.307 --> 00:19:53.560
Is that the summit
of our ambition, really?

339
00:19:53.643 --> 00:19:56.437
Okay.
You think you can do better?

340
00:19:56.980 --> 00:20:01.067
Tomorrow, Bruins' playing Golden Knights,
Cold War classic at TD Garden.

341
00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.194
Dave, you're my guy,
so you're covering the game.

342
00:20:03.278 --> 00:20:05.947
And I want the two of you on the tailgate.

343
00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.575
So tell me, how are you gonna
get people talking about us?

344
00:20:08.658 --> 00:20:11.161
Actually, I was thinking,
instead of covering the tailgate,

345
00:20:11.244 --> 00:20:12.328
we could do a segment

346
00:20:12.412 --> 00:20:15.039
on the team donating coats
to the city's homeless youth.

347
00:20:15.123 --> 00:20:17.667
I'm sorry, what's your name?
I don't care. You are boring.

348
00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.086
- I am bored. You have bored me.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[BUZZER SOUNDS]</font></b>

349
00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:23.381
Look at this guy.
2008 called. Wants its haircut back.

350
00:20:23.464 --> 00:20:26.885
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b> Actually, the numbers
on his hair are huge.

351
00:20:26.968 --> 00:20:29.679
And his face and his smile.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>

352
00:20:30.221 --> 00:20:32.599
You should give your head
a pat on the back.

353
00:20:32.682 --> 00:20:33.850
Way to go, head.

354
00:20:33.933 --> 00:20:36.060
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Ooh!
- She oughta be committed.

355
00:20:36.144 --> 00:20:39.022
Oh, I am. Totally committed.

356
00:20:42.275 --> 00:20:45.361
What if we shoot B-roll
of everyone cooking in the parking lot,

357
00:20:45.445 --> 00:20:48.573
and we do a whole "Is there salmonella
at the tailgate" kinda thing?

358
00:20:48.656 --> 00:20:51.701
- Go on.
- Uh, or, uh, face paint.

359
00:20:52.327 --> 00:20:53.620
Uh, on fans' faces.

360
00:20:54.037 --> 00:20:56.623
"Is it poisoning fans?
Find out at 11:00."

361
00:20:56.706 --> 00:20:59.626
- Face paint isn't poisonous.
- Yeah. And we'll tell them that at 11:00.

362
00:21:00.043 --> 00:21:02.962
Good.
That doesn't totally suck.

363
00:21:03.046 --> 00:21:05.965
All right, people, I just want you
to focus on what's important. Okay?

364
00:21:06.049 --> 00:21:08.468
And that's fourth place.
All right?

365
00:21:08.551 --> 00:21:10.470
Oh, I'm sorry, are we keeping you?

366
00:21:10.553 --> 00:21:11.971
I hope you're not running anywhere

367
00:21:12.055 --> 00:21:15.141
without re-editing that pumpkin debacle
for the 7:00 p.m. show.

368
00:21:16.184 --> 00:21:17.227
Thank you.

369
00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:18.311
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHATTER]</font></b>

370
00:21:19.062 --> 00:21:22.398
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b> Can't we do better
than face paint and salmonella?

371
00:21:22.482 --> 00:21:24.400
Yeah. Let's make it E. coli.

372
00:21:24.484 --> 00:21:28.279
Come on, Mack. I'm serious. If we found
some stories that were inspiring,

373
00:21:28.363 --> 00:21:30.281
we could light a fire under this place.

374
00:21:30.365 --> 00:21:32.200
I can't afford to lose this job.

375
00:21:35.036 --> 00:21:36.079
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>

376
00:21:41.084 --> 00:21:42.627
- Me again!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[YELPS]</font></b>

377
00:21:43.253 --> 00:21:45.129
- It's me, Eleanor.
- This is getting...

378
00:21:45.213 --> 00:21:47.423
- Okay, okay.
- I'm your Fairy Godmother.

379
00:21:47.507 --> 00:21:49.050
Just back off, lady!

380
00:21:49.133 --> 00:21:51.094
I know what you're thinking,
and it's true.

381
00:21:51.177 --> 00:21:53.096
Most Fairy Godmothers are a lot older.

382
00:21:53.179 --> 00:21:55.974
If you can overlook my youth
and your total lack of experience,

383
00:21:56.057 --> 00:21:59.435
you'll find I have a real can-do attitude
that's gonna take us very, very far.

384
00:21:59.519 --> 00:22:01.938
- I will call 911.
- Oh, I'll show you.

385
00:22:02.939 --> 00:22:05.441
No. Please wait. No, please don't.
I have kids.

386
00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:07.861
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

387
00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:12.323
<b><font color="#ca004b">[EXCLAIMS]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Huh?

388
00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:16.327
- Oh!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

389
00:22:17.328 --> 00:22:18.705
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS AND GRUNTS]</font></b>

390
00:22:20.707 --> 00:22:21.749
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

391
00:22:22.542 --> 00:22:23.751
What just happened?

392
00:22:23.835 --> 00:22:26.045
I was trying for a ball gown.

393
00:22:26.129 --> 00:22:29.424
It's not my best work,
but at least it's weather appropriate?

394
00:22:30.133 --> 00:22:33.678
Oh, my God, it's happening.
I'm finally losing my mind.

395
00:22:33.761 --> 00:22:37.015
Don't be silly. This is magic?

396
00:22:38.558 --> 00:22:41.394
Yo, Mack, what's the occasion?

397
00:22:41.477 --> 00:22:43.730
Wait, Ray, you can see this?

398
00:22:43.813 --> 00:22:45.815
Uh, it's kinda hard to miss.

399
00:22:47.650 --> 00:22:48.693
You look hot.

400
00:22:49.569 --> 00:22:52.197
You're not supposed to say
that kinda thing in the workplace.

401
00:22:52.280 --> 00:22:54.782
I mean, your face is all red and sweaty.

402
00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:57.994
Oh, my God, he saw it. It's real.

403
00:22:58.077 --> 00:22:59.412
Of course it is.

404
00:22:59.496 --> 00:23:01.206
Now, do you have a carriage here,

405
00:23:01.289 --> 00:23:03.416
or shall we hitch a ride
in someone else's pumpkin?

406
00:23:04.375 --> 00:23:06.211
- Shh, that's Grant, my boss.
- What...

407
00:23:06.294 --> 00:23:08.087
- He can't see me like this!
- Oh!

408
00:23:08.171 --> 00:23:09.172
Why?

409
00:23:09.255 --> 00:23:11.716
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Because you poofed me
into a sleeping bag.

410
00:23:12.717 --> 00:23:13.718
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CAR ALARM CHIRPS]</font></b>

411
00:23:15.261 --> 00:23:16.888
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ALARM BEEPING]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[BRAKES SCREECHING]</font></b>

412
00:23:18.765 --> 00:23:20.934
- Okay, don't press. Can you...
- What is that?

413
00:23:21.017 --> 00:23:22.953
- Hang on...
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ON RADIO]</font></b> <b><font color="#cf685c">MAN:</font></b> 96.1 Classic Radio...

414
00:23:22.977 --> 00:23:23.978
Who's talking?

415
00:23:24.062 --> 00:23:26.189
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[BEEPING]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[TIRES SCREECHING]</font></b>

416
00:23:26.272 --> 00:23:27.357
- Just... Okay.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>

417
00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:28.650
It looks like me!

418
00:23:28.733 --> 00:23:30.527
Yeah... Oh, my God. Okay, listen.

419
00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:32.904
I'm gonna drop you at the South Station,

420
00:23:32.987 --> 00:23:35.323
and you can get on a Greyhound

421
00:23:35.406 --> 00:23:37.659
and head back
to wherever it is you came from.

422
00:23:37.742 --> 00:23:39.410
What... Did you say a greyhound?

423
00:23:39.494 --> 00:23:40.912
Yeah, a Greyhound bus.

424
00:23:41.412 --> 00:23:44.082
- They're turning greyhounds into buses?
- Uh...

425
00:23:44.165 --> 00:23:47.585
- Typically, they just become footmen.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[FESTIVE MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO]</font></b>

426
00:23:47.669 --> 00:23:50.171
Actually, they would be
faster than a pumpkin.

427
00:23:50.255 --> 00:23:52.340
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[DANCE MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO]</font></b>
- Okay. Stop! Stop.

428
00:23:52.674 --> 00:23:54.801
Don't you have somewhere else
that you can go?

429
00:23:54.884 --> 00:23:56.928
No. Not locally.

430
00:23:57.428 --> 00:24:00.473
Oh, Except for those lovely princes
in the alley

431
00:24:00.557 --> 00:24:02.016
said that I could stay with them,

432
00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.811
as long as I didn't mind
sharing knitting needles.

433
00:24:04.894 --> 00:24:05.895
Okay.

434
00:24:05.979 --> 00:24:08.189
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[FESTIVE MUSIC RESUMES PLAYING]</font></b>
- All right. Here...

435
00:24:08.273 --> 00:24:10.692
Take this money
and just get yourself something to eat.

436
00:24:10.775 --> 00:24:13.027
Oh, thank you.
I am really hungry.

437
00:24:15.363 --> 00:24:18.283
- Oh, it's hard and thin.
- Wait, stop! Spit it out!

438
00:24:18.366 --> 00:24:20.201
Spit it. Ew.

439
00:24:20.285 --> 00:24:23.454
No, this is money.
Then you can go and stay in a hotel.

440
00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:26.666
I'm sorry, but you have to go.

441
00:24:28.668 --> 00:24:29.711
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> What...

442
00:24:29.794 --> 00:24:31.087
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Out you go.

443
00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:33.173
Wait.

444
00:24:35.133 --> 00:24:36.676
What about your dearest wish?

445
00:24:36.759 --> 00:24:39.804
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b> What dearest wish?
What are you talking about?

446
00:24:50.607 --> 00:24:51.608
See?

447
00:24:52.817 --> 00:24:53.985
Where did you get this?

448
00:24:54.736 --> 00:24:57.488
Well, you sent it to me when you were ten.

449
00:25:16.799 --> 00:25:17.842
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR GRUNTS]</font></b>

450
00:25:20.303 --> 00:25:22.430
Why have we stopped at this hovel?

451
00:25:22.514 --> 00:25:24.724
Shouldn't we proceed directly
to the castle?

452
00:25:24.807 --> 00:25:26.911
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b> This is the castle. I live here.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CAR HONKS]</font></b>

453
00:25:26.935 --> 00:25:29.145
Real estate prices must be
much more expensive in Boston

454
00:25:29.229 --> 00:25:30.647
than they are in Motherland.

455
00:25:30.730 --> 00:25:33.066
Hey. You can stay for one night.

456
00:25:36.277 --> 00:25:38.863
Oh, something has my gown.

457
00:25:38.947 --> 00:25:40.907
You are not meeting my kids.

458
00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:43.868
Can't you just puff yourself
an igloo or something?

459
00:25:43.952 --> 00:25:46.454
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
Oh, ice castle construction?

460
00:25:46.538 --> 00:25:48.414
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
Oh, I wish.

461
00:25:53.503 --> 00:25:55.505
You're putting me in the dungeon?

462
00:26:04.430 --> 00:26:06.474
- Not a dungeon.
- Huh?

463
00:26:07.225 --> 00:26:08.893
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> It's a basement.

464
00:26:12.480 --> 00:26:14.983
- Stay here and be quiet.
- Got it.

465
00:26:16.276 --> 00:26:17.861
Okay. Get me out of this.

466
00:26:17.944 --> 00:26:18.945
Right.

467
00:26:19.904 --> 00:26:20.947
Of course.

468
00:26:22.323 --> 00:26:24.409
Here we go.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

469
00:26:25.326 --> 00:26:28.955
Funny story, I might not
quite remember how to poof you back.

470
00:26:31.749 --> 00:26:32.750
Great.

471
00:26:36.462 --> 00:26:37.463
Sorry.

472
00:26:37.964 --> 00:26:39.591
<b><font color="#ca004b">[DOOR CLOSES]</font></b>

473
00:26:42.427 --> 00:26:43.428
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS AND YELPS]</font></b>

474
00:26:50.602 --> 00:26:51.603
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

475
00:26:57.025 --> 00:26:58.026
<b><font color="#ca004b">[EXCLAIMS]</font></b>

476
00:27:01.321 --> 00:27:03.781
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING]</font></b>
This is the song you sing

477
00:27:03.865 --> 00:27:05.950
When you're in the dungeon

478
00:27:07.577 --> 00:27:11.623
This is the basement dungeon song you sing

479
00:27:12.373 --> 00:27:14.250
Police are not ruling out witchcraft

480
00:27:14.334 --> 00:27:17.962
in what is now being called
the Essex Pumpkin Cult Massacre.

481
00:27:18.505 --> 00:27:19.857
Coming up next, we're gonna show you

482
00:27:19.881 --> 00:27:21.883
- how to turn a pinecone...
- Hey.

483
00:27:21.966 --> 00:27:23.343
...into your favorite celebrity.

484
00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:24.761
Hey, Bingo.

485
00:27:25.220 --> 00:27:27.555
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ON TV]</font></b> <b><font color="#cf685c">BARB:</font></b> I know who mine is.
Chris Pine.

486
00:27:27.847 --> 00:27:30.892
Coming up later,
Mass General Neurosurgery Department...

487
00:27:30.975 --> 00:27:32.036
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE EXCLAIMS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[THUD]</font></b>

488
00:27:32.060 --> 00:27:34.038
...gets a new head,
and you won't believe his name.

489
00:27:34.062 --> 00:27:36.439
- Sorry I'm late. Again.
- Ryan Brain.

490
00:27:37.857 --> 00:27:41.528
Ah, I see everyone is still wide awake
and watching TV.

491
00:27:41.611 --> 00:27:43.530
Only thing that would make this better

492
00:27:43.613 --> 00:27:47.408
is if you'd had pizza for dinner
and you hadn't done your homework.

493
00:27:47.617 --> 00:27:50.620
Wow, it's like you've been here
with us this whole time.

494
00:27:50.703 --> 00:27:52.372
Well, the pizza had vegetables on it.

495
00:27:52.455 --> 00:27:54.499
<b><font color="#cf685c">MIA:</font></b> We didn't eat them,
but they were there.

496
00:27:54.582 --> 00:27:56.251
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
What are you wearing?

497
00:27:56.334 --> 00:27:59.420
- Um, it was for a story.
- Ah.

498
00:28:00.171 --> 00:28:01.548
Hey, how was your spelling test?

499
00:28:02.507 --> 00:28:04.551
- I failed.
- What?

500
00:28:04.634 --> 00:28:07.595
But I quizzed you on it last night.
You got 100%.

501
00:28:07.679 --> 00:28:11.224
So, you know that I know the same thing
as the people who got an A.

502
00:28:11.724 --> 00:28:14.352
- Ha, ha. Bed. Now.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b>

503
00:28:14.435 --> 00:28:16.020
- Good night.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MIA:</font></b> Good night.

504
00:28:16.104 --> 00:28:18.940
- Good night, Bingo.
- Hey.

505
00:28:19.440 --> 00:28:20.984
- Hey.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> Mom.

506
00:28:21.067 --> 00:28:23.486
A middle-aged woman is on a rope
swinging over a river.

507
00:28:23.570 --> 00:28:26.906
I think everybody knows how
that's gonna end. How was your day?

508
00:28:26.990 --> 00:28:27.991
It was fine.

509
00:28:30.869 --> 00:28:33.454
Mr. Clancy wants her to sing a solo
for show choir.

510
00:28:33.538 --> 00:28:35.415
- Paula.
- Well, it's exciting.

511
00:28:35.498 --> 00:28:37.167
But you're not in show choir.

512
00:28:37.250 --> 00:28:41.087
No, but Kent Buckus is.
Only he got mono.

513
00:28:41.171 --> 00:28:44.299
Now, half the choir's out sick,
including Kim Murphy.

514
00:28:44.382 --> 00:28:49.888
So, now Mr. Clancy wants me to
sing Kim's solo at the parade next week.

515
00:28:49.971 --> 00:28:50.972
What parade?

516
00:28:51.431 --> 00:28:53.308
The big holiday parade downtown.

517
00:28:53.558 --> 00:28:55.560
Did you tell him you don't wanna do it?

518
00:28:57.520 --> 00:28:59.647
Yeah, I'm going to.
It's a dumb idea.

519
00:29:00.690 --> 00:29:04.152
Uh... Look, it's not a dumb idea.

520
00:29:04.235 --> 00:29:06.529
It's just...
They'd be lucky to have you.

521
00:29:06.613 --> 00:29:08.489
There's a reason
you didn't join show choir.

522
00:29:08.573 --> 00:29:10.950
Yeah, I know. It's fine.
Forget it. I'm going to bed.

523
00:29:11.493 --> 00:29:13.077
- <b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Night, babe.
- Night.

524
00:29:13.578 --> 00:29:15.288
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Good night. I love you.

525
00:29:16.748 --> 00:29:17.874
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>

526
00:29:17.957 --> 00:29:19.459
I bet when Beyoncé was young,

527
00:29:19.542 --> 00:29:22.212
her mother used to encourage her
in exactly the same way.

528
00:29:27.091 --> 00:29:30.845
Did Beyoncé hyperventilate so badly
in her eighth-grade talent show

529
00:29:30.929 --> 00:29:32.972
that she passed out and cracked a rib?

530
00:29:33.056 --> 00:29:34.516
In seventh grade, it was hives.

531
00:29:34.599 --> 00:29:37.018
She scratched those scabs
so badly they got infected,

532
00:29:37.101 --> 00:29:39.229
I had to take her
to the hospital at 2:00 a.m.

533
00:29:39.312 --> 00:29:41.856
She had a fever of 103.
Doctor said she could have got sepsis.

534
00:29:41.940 --> 00:29:44.067
If you ever get sick of your job
as a TV producer,

535
00:29:44.150 --> 00:29:45.985
you could become a motivational speaker.

536
00:29:46.069 --> 00:29:48.488
Sixth grade, she projectile vomited
before she got onstage.

537
00:29:48.571 --> 00:29:51.282
Every time she goes to perform,
it's a complete disaster.

538
00:29:51.366 --> 00:29:53.159
She ends up totally crushed.

539
00:29:53.243 --> 00:29:54.369
You sound like Mom.

540
00:29:54.452 --> 00:29:56.037
Well, Mom has common sense.

541
00:29:56.830 --> 00:29:58.414
Mom didn't raise Beyoncé.

542
00:30:17.141 --> 00:30:18.226
Oh!
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]</font></b>

543
00:30:25.525 --> 00:30:26.526
What are you doing?

544
00:30:27.026 --> 00:30:28.111
Oh.

545
00:30:28.194 --> 00:30:30.655
- Is this your true love?
- Not anymore.

546
00:30:30.989 --> 00:30:32.991
What? What do you mean?

547
00:30:33.074 --> 00:30:35.743
Step three says
that you find your true love

548
00:30:35.827 --> 00:30:37.453
and you live happily ever after.

549
00:30:38.204 --> 00:30:39.956
Well, we did live happily.

550
00:30:41.916 --> 00:30:43.668
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>
But life isn't always a fairy tale.

551
00:30:44.169 --> 00:30:47.755
Sometimes people grow
or change or get divorced

552
00:30:47.839 --> 00:30:50.091
or fall out of love
or run off and join a cult

553
00:30:50.175 --> 00:30:52.802
or fall in love
with a skinny Pilates instructor.

554
00:30:53.178 --> 00:30:55.763
Life isn't as simple
as "happily ever after."

555
00:30:56.514 --> 00:30:57.515
But it has to be.

556
00:30:57.599 --> 00:31:00.643
I came all this way to help you
find your heart's desire.

557
00:31:00.727 --> 00:31:03.104
My heart's desire now
would be a clean house

558
00:31:03.188 --> 00:31:07.317
and maybe the eyebrows that I had
before I started stress plucking.

559
00:31:09.194 --> 00:31:11.362
That's the saddest thing I've ever heard.

560
00:31:13.656 --> 00:31:14.699
What happened...

561
00:31:15.408 --> 00:31:18.703
What happened to the little girl
that wrote me this letter?

562
00:31:20.538 --> 00:31:21.956
I guess she grew up.

563
00:31:22.373 --> 00:31:24.000
Do you want me to make your bed?

564
00:31:25.001 --> 00:31:26.419
No, I already did it.

565
00:31:31.758 --> 00:31:33.760
Don't root around in any of my boxes.

566
00:31:34.177 --> 00:31:36.095
All right. Good night.

567
00:31:43.102 --> 00:31:44.354
No, thank you.

568
00:31:45.939 --> 00:31:46.940
<b><font color="#ca004b">[DOOR CLOSES]</font></b>

569
00:32:13.091 --> 00:32:14.843
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BIRDS CHIRPING]</font></b>

570
00:32:16.469 --> 00:32:19.097
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Uh-oh, kids, here comes Moira.

571
00:32:19.180 --> 00:32:23.017
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[MOIRA CLEARS THROAT]</font></b>
- Pretending like everything's still fine.

572
00:32:23.101 --> 00:32:25.395
Let us open our texts, shall we?

573
00:32:27.438 --> 00:32:31.025
Now, the role of a Fairy Godmother is...

574
00:32:36.573 --> 00:32:37.574
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALARM BUZZING]</font></b>

575
00:32:45.874 --> 00:32:46.875
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALARM STOPS]</font></b>

576
00:33:00.138 --> 00:33:01.139
<b><font color="#ca004b">[YAWNS]</font></b>

577
00:33:01.764 --> 00:33:02.765
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

578
00:33:02.849 --> 00:33:05.018
- Good morning, friend.
- How did you get in here?

579
00:33:05.101 --> 00:33:08.646
Oh, hey, now they look just great.
Like two little fox tails.

580
00:33:08.730 --> 00:33:09.930
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> What?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

581
00:33:12.901 --> 00:33:15.236
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
What have you done to my eyebrows?

582
00:33:17.572 --> 00:33:19.449
What have you done to my house?

583
00:33:19.532 --> 00:33:20.867
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

584
00:33:22.452 --> 00:33:23.786
Last night, I did some thinking.

585
00:33:23.870 --> 00:33:25.872
I know you don't believe
in happily ever after,

586
00:33:25.955 --> 00:33:27.081
but that's why I'm here.

587
00:33:27.165 --> 00:33:30.376
And if we're going to find it for you,
you'll need a castle.

588
00:33:30.460 --> 00:33:32.295
The hovel won't work.

589
00:33:32.378 --> 00:33:34.672
You turned it into Medieval Times.

590
00:33:34.756 --> 00:33:36.007
I know, right?

591
00:33:36.090 --> 00:33:37.091
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTING]</font></b>

592
00:33:40.553 --> 00:33:41.554
- Oh...
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[PIG GRUNTING]</font></b>

593
00:33:43.806 --> 00:33:45.892
Oh, my God, Bingo?

594
00:33:45.975 --> 00:33:47.852
Bingo, is that you?
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

595
00:33:48.436 --> 00:33:50.063
You turned my dog into a pig?

596
00:33:50.146 --> 00:33:52.023
Technically, he's a piglet.

597
00:33:52.106 --> 00:33:54.275
I was trying for a woodland creature

598
00:33:54.359 --> 00:33:56.945
to help out with
all this housework, obviously,

599
00:33:57.028 --> 00:33:58.780
but then the spell got away from me.

600
00:33:58.863 --> 00:34:01.324
You need to put everything back
exactly the way that it was.

601
00:34:01.407 --> 00:34:03.368
I'm serious.
I don't want a castle.

602
00:34:03.451 --> 00:34:06.204
I really don't want my kids
finding out I have a Fairy Godmother.

603
00:34:07.705 --> 00:34:10.041
Oh. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]</font></b>
Hi, girls.

604
00:34:11.125 --> 00:34:12.126
Oh!

605
00:34:12.627 --> 00:34:13.670
Hi.

606
00:34:13.753 --> 00:34:14.754
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTING]</font></b>

607
00:34:16.047 --> 00:34:18.049
- Huh? Bingo?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[DOOR CLOSES]</font></b>

608
00:34:18.132 --> 00:34:19.926
<b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Who wants bagels?

609
00:34:20.009 --> 00:34:22.178
Whoa, what did you do to your house?

610
00:34:23.096 --> 00:34:26.349
Whoa! <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
What did you do to your eyebrows?

611
00:34:26.432 --> 00:34:27.934
Mom has a Fairy Godmother.

612
00:34:28.017 --> 00:34:31.396
No, uh, Eleanor is a set decorator
from the station.

613
00:34:31.479 --> 00:34:32.897
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ANIMAL CHITTERING]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL SCREAM]</font></b>

614
00:34:32.981 --> 00:34:35.316
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b> <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> There you are!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERS]</font></b>

615
00:34:35.400 --> 00:34:36.693
Where have you been?

616
00:34:36.776 --> 00:34:38.444
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GIRLS SCREAM]</font></b>

617
00:34:38.528 --> 00:34:41.573
Oh, it's okay.
He's just here to help with the housework.

618
00:34:42.198 --> 00:34:45.076
Oh, right.
Does he do laundry as well?

619
00:34:45.160 --> 00:34:48.454
I'd keep him away
from your clothes. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

620
00:34:49.372 --> 00:34:51.499
Raccoons are best for light work.

621
00:34:51.583 --> 00:34:53.459
- They're very good with brooms...
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERS]</font></b>

622
00:34:54.252 --> 00:34:56.754
Uh, dusting and sweeping.

623
00:34:59.215 --> 00:35:01.551
How did you just do that with the broom?

624
00:35:01.634 --> 00:35:05.221
Magic. Levitation is something
I've really been working on.

625
00:35:05.305 --> 00:35:07.849
- Can you magic me a new iPad?
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Sure.

626
00:35:10.351 --> 00:35:12.770
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
One eye patch, as requested.

627
00:35:12.854 --> 00:35:15.481
Wait, can we just take it back to the fact

628
00:35:15.565 --> 00:35:18.568
that there is a raccoon
sweeping your kitchen?

629
00:35:18.693 --> 00:35:20.236
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Mmm-hmm.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERING]</font></b>

630
00:35:20.320 --> 00:35:22.197
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> His name is Gary, by the way.

631
00:35:23.198 --> 00:35:24.199
You know what?

632
00:35:24.282 --> 00:35:27.243
I don't understand what's going on,
but, uh, it's going on Facebook.

633
00:35:27.327 --> 00:35:30.079
Uh, are you crazy?
They'll cart us off to a rubber room.

634
00:35:30.163 --> 00:35:33.500
To be honest,
I'm not really supposed to be here either.

635
00:35:33.583 --> 00:35:36.753
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b> If my headmistress Moira,
back at the Motherland,

636
00:35:36.836 --> 00:35:38.522
found out about this...
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]</font></b>

637
00:35:38.546 --> 00:35:40.173
Oof! It'd be a disaster.

638
00:35:40.715 --> 00:35:42.967
Right. We don't want
her Fairy Godmother boss

639
00:35:43.051 --> 00:35:45.053
back at the Motherland to find out.

640
00:35:45.136 --> 00:35:47.764
- <b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Uh-huh.
- So, Eleanor's gonna go back today, right?

641
00:35:47.847 --> 00:35:49.825
- Right. Eleanor's gonna... Wait. What?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GARY SNEEZES]</font></b>

642
00:35:49.849 --> 00:35:52.268
No, I can't leave until I help you.

643
00:35:52.352 --> 00:35:54.145
I don't...
<b><font color="#ca004b">[LOUDLY]</font></b> ...need any help!

644
00:35:54.229 --> 00:35:55.230
Are you kidding?

645
00:35:55.313 --> 00:35:57.899
All you do is complain
about how stressed you are.

646
00:35:57.982 --> 00:36:00.401
- She's always tired.
- And grumpy.

647
00:36:00.818 --> 00:36:03.988
No, that is not totally true.

648
00:36:04.280 --> 00:36:05.281
Is it?

649
00:36:05.907 --> 00:36:06.908
Uh...

650
00:36:06.991 --> 00:36:10.453
So, she can stay?
Please, please!

651
00:36:10.537 --> 00:36:12.622
- Please, Mom.
- Please.

652
00:36:12.705 --> 00:36:14.666
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE SIGHS]</font></b>
- Please! Please!

653
00:36:14.749 --> 00:36:16.626
- Okay.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

654
00:36:16.709 --> 00:36:19.754
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Okay, you guys have gotta get to school,
and I gotta get to work.

655
00:36:19.838 --> 00:36:22.841
And... Are you gonna
be okay here by yourself?

656
00:36:22.924 --> 00:36:25.718
Oh, sure.
Gary and I can work on a moat.

657
00:36:26.427 --> 00:36:28.555
You know,
maybe you can come to work with me...

658
00:36:28.638 --> 00:36:31.850
- Oh!
- ...but first fix my eyebrows, please.

659
00:36:31.975 --> 00:36:35.728
<b><font color="#cf685c">COMMENTATOR:</font></b> Welcome to the Cold War Classic.

660
00:36:36.187 --> 00:36:40.483
The Boston Bruins
versus the Golden Knights.

661
00:36:40.692 --> 00:36:44.153
Go, Bruins!

662
00:36:44.237 --> 00:36:46.077
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHATTER]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

663
00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:56.499
Here.
Put this on and try to fit in.

664
00:36:57.750 --> 00:37:00.128
If you do any magic,
I'll lock you in the trunk.

665
00:37:02.589 --> 00:37:03.590
Hey, guys.

666
00:37:04.215 --> 00:37:06.384
Ah, look who's here.

667
00:37:06.467 --> 00:37:07.760
Yeah, guys, sorry I'm late.

668
00:37:07.844 --> 00:37:11.306
It was a crazy day.
This is my cousin, Eleanor.

669
00:37:11.389 --> 00:37:12.640
Oh, I'm actually her Fairy...

670
00:37:12.724 --> 00:37:16.102
Favorite cousin. She's visiting,
and so I said she could tag along.

671
00:37:16.978 --> 00:37:19.731
Ah. Hiya, I'm Duff, on camera.

672
00:37:20.190 --> 00:37:23.193
Duff Oncamera.
What a lovely name.

673
00:37:23.276 --> 00:37:25.904
Oh, wow.
Look at all this stuff.

674
00:37:25.987 --> 00:37:27.739
You must have the strength of a giant

675
00:37:27.822 --> 00:37:30.825
and the brains of a wizard
to be in charge of all this.

676
00:37:30.909 --> 00:37:32.410
Nice to meet you.
I'm Hugh Prince.

677
00:37:32.494 --> 00:37:33.495
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

678
00:37:35.580 --> 00:37:36.998
<b><font color="#ca004b">[WHISPERS]</font></b> Prince.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

679
00:37:38.374 --> 00:37:40.460
I like your costume.
You must be a huge fan.

680
00:37:40.543 --> 00:37:41.544
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHEERING]</font></b>

681
00:37:41.628 --> 00:37:43.505
<b><font color="#cf685c">MAN #1:</font></b> Go, Bruins!
<b><font color="#cf685c">MAN #2:</font></b> You go, baby! You go!

682
00:37:43.588 --> 00:37:45.215
Yes. Go, Brains!

683
00:37:45.298 --> 00:37:46.633
Bruins.

684
00:37:46.758 --> 00:37:48.676
- Hmm?
- Bruins.

685
00:37:49.052 --> 00:37:51.804
- Bruins. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
- Bruins. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b> So funny.

686
00:37:52.514 --> 00:37:53.765
I like her already.

687
00:37:56.684 --> 00:37:59.062
- You sure you don't need any help?
- <b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Thanks.

688
00:37:59.145 --> 00:38:01.314
But dealing with this camera
is literally my job.

689
00:38:01.397 --> 00:38:03.650
- Hmm.
- What do you do?

690
00:38:03.733 --> 00:38:05.944
Oh, I help people find
their happily ever after.

691
00:38:06.402 --> 00:38:09.030
- You must be from California.
- Hmm.

692
00:38:13.993 --> 00:38:17.622
I was thinkin' we could do a story about
the organization's effort to recycle.

693
00:38:17.705 --> 00:38:19.791
They're leading the way
for households...

694
00:38:19.874 --> 00:38:20.875
We could do that.

695
00:38:20.959 --> 00:38:23.920
Next month, we'll be living
in a storm drain, drinking sewer water

696
00:38:24.003 --> 00:38:25.547
and eating roadkill to survive,

697
00:38:25.630 --> 00:38:27.131
because Grant would've fired us.

698
00:38:27.215 --> 00:38:29.384
There are some guys
having an eating contest,

699
00:38:29.467 --> 00:38:32.595
shoving chili dogs down their masks,
which can be pretty gross.

700
00:38:32.679 --> 00:38:34.597
Yeah, and if we get lucky
and someone chokes,

701
00:38:34.681 --> 00:38:36.558
we could even do a story on killer chili.

702
00:38:36.641 --> 00:38:37.976
We could only dream.

703
00:38:38.059 --> 00:38:41.062
Meantime, I'll go look
for people eating undercooked wings.

704
00:38:41.145 --> 00:38:42.355
Great.

705
00:38:43.231 --> 00:38:45.233
- Go, Brains!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

706
00:38:45.316 --> 00:38:47.068
Oh, my Godmothers.

707
00:38:47.193 --> 00:38:50.196
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b> That Hugh Prince
is so handsome and nice.

708
00:38:50.280 --> 00:38:53.616
And according to Duff, he's not living
happily ever after with anyone.

709
00:38:53.700 --> 00:38:55.577
Enough with the "happily ever after."

710
00:38:55.660 --> 00:38:57.328
I have to work, Eleanor, please.

711
00:38:58.163 --> 00:39:01.583
Why don't you help me?
Why don't you... Oh!

712
00:39:01.666 --> 00:39:03.418
You see these hot pots of chowder...

713
00:39:03.501 --> 00:39:05.420
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Mmm-hmm.
- ...all over the tailgate?

714
00:39:05.503 --> 00:39:09.465
Why don't you go try 'em and report back
and tell me which one is your favorite?

715
00:39:09.549 --> 00:39:11.384
Cauldrons of magical concoctions?

716
00:39:11.467 --> 00:39:12.844
- Yes!
- I won't let you down.

717
00:39:14.387 --> 00:39:15.388
Oh!

718
00:39:19.309 --> 00:39:20.435
Mmm!

719
00:39:25.064 --> 00:39:26.482
Mmm!

720
00:39:28.568 --> 00:39:29.611
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

721
00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:33.281
Mmm!

722
00:39:34.199 --> 00:39:35.241
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUFFLED]</font></b>
Thank you.

723
00:39:35.492 --> 00:39:36.493
<b><font color="#cf685c">MAN:</font></b> You're welcome.

724
00:39:40.038 --> 00:39:41.080
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT CHATTER]</font></b>

725
00:39:42.832 --> 00:39:44.834
Notify the Pulitzer Committee.

726
00:39:46.127 --> 00:39:48.046
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR BREATHING HEAVILY]</font></b>
- Wait, is that...

727
00:39:48.129 --> 00:39:49.214
Is that Eleanor?

728
00:39:49.339 --> 00:39:50.340
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BREATHING HEAVILY]</font></b>

729
00:39:50.882 --> 00:39:52.133
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Eleanor?

730
00:39:52.217 --> 00:39:53.426
- Wait.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> Hi.

731
00:39:53.510 --> 00:39:55.887
- Eleanor. Eleanor, is everything okay?
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Hey.

732
00:39:55.970 --> 00:39:56.971
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUFFLED]</font></b>
Oh, yes.

733
00:39:57.055 --> 00:39:59.140
- It's just a little hard to breathe.
- Oh, okay.

734
00:39:59.224 --> 00:40:01.142
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Mmm-hmm.
- Is face paint poisonous?

735
00:40:01.226 --> 00:40:02.506
- No...
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Look at her!

736
00:40:02.560 --> 00:40:04.771
This is what I look like
after I have shellfish.

737
00:40:04.854 --> 00:40:06.397
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Oh.
- You had any seafood?

738
00:40:06.481 --> 00:40:10.193
Not really. Just six bowls of chowder
and 18 lobster rolls...

739
00:40:10.276 --> 00:40:11.277
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> No.
<b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> Oh...

740
00:40:11.361 --> 00:40:13.112
- <b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> That's bad.
- I have this for later.

741
00:40:13.196 --> 00:40:14.239
- <b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> No!
- No! Okay.

742
00:40:14.322 --> 00:40:16.616
There's an EpiPen in the van,
and we'll get the winner.

743
00:40:17.200 --> 00:40:19.577
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPING]</font></b> It's really
getting hard to breathe now.

744
00:40:20.078 --> 00:40:22.747
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b> I got it.
- Oh, good.

745
00:40:23.289 --> 00:40:24.290
Okay.

746
00:40:25.250 --> 00:40:26.793
Uh, there's no instructions.

747
00:40:27.168 --> 00:40:31.089
I'm just gonna pop the cap off this, and
then, uh, jam the needle into your thigh.

748
00:40:31.172 --> 00:40:32.715
Needle?
You said it was a pen?

749
00:40:32.799 --> 00:40:34.259
Eleanor, you need this!

750
00:40:34.342 --> 00:40:36.970
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> No, needle! No, no, no!
- Eleanor! Eleanor!

751
00:40:37.053 --> 00:40:39.138
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BOTH SHOUTING]</font></b>

752
00:40:39.305 --> 00:40:40.807
Eleanor, you need this! Please!

753
00:40:40.890 --> 00:40:42.976
- No, needle!
- Look, there's a unicorn!

754
00:40:43.059 --> 00:40:44.352
- Where?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE GRUNTS]</font></b>

755
00:40:45.061 --> 00:40:46.479
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>
No!

756
00:40:46.563 --> 00:40:47.564
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SHOUTING IN LATIN]</font></b>

757
00:40:49.023 --> 00:40:50.024
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]</font></b>

758
00:40:57.574 --> 00:41:00.160
Mayhem today outside the Bruins game.

759
00:41:00.243 --> 00:41:02.662
Channel 8's Hugh Prince was on the scene.

760
00:41:02.745 --> 00:41:05.790
All right, city officials tell us
no fireworks were planned

761
00:41:05.874 --> 00:41:08.751
and they have no explanation
for what's happening.

762
00:41:08.835 --> 00:41:10.879
However, local authorities believe

763
00:41:10.962 --> 00:41:15.341
the event may be caused
by an unusual weather phenomenon.

764
00:41:15.425 --> 00:41:18.011
And what about reports
that it might've been

765
00:41:18.094 --> 00:41:20.346
some sort of military space weapon?

766
00:41:20.847 --> 00:41:25.560
I have not heard about a space weapon.
Do you have a source for those reports?

767
00:41:25.643 --> 00:41:27.437
- No. But as soon as we do...
- Thanks, Barb.

768
00:41:27.520 --> 00:41:29.772
...you can bet
that we will update this story.

769
00:41:29.856 --> 00:41:30.899
Space weapon?

770
00:41:30.982 --> 00:41:32.859
Thank you, Hugh.
Please stay safe out there.

771
00:41:38.156 --> 00:41:39.157
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CAR HONKS]</font></b>

772
00:41:39.699 --> 00:41:41.993
You mean well, but this isn't gonna work.

773
00:41:42.076 --> 00:41:44.913
What? No, it's only been one day.

774
00:41:44.996 --> 00:41:46.998
And my house looks like Game of Thrones,

775
00:41:47.081 --> 00:41:50.001
you turned my dog into a piglet,
you almost blew up the Bruins.

776
00:41:50.084 --> 00:41:52.003
Well, because you stabbed me.

777
00:41:52.086 --> 00:41:55.256
I saved your life.
Who eats that much seafood?

778
00:41:56.424 --> 00:41:57.550
Sharks!

779
00:41:57.634 --> 00:41:59.177
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> It's late.

780
00:41:59.260 --> 00:42:01.930
You can stay one more night,
but you're gone in the morning.

781
00:42:02.972 --> 00:42:05.850
Meanwhile, events on the ice
are just as remarkable...

782
00:42:05.934 --> 00:42:07.060
Eleanor! Hi!

783
00:42:07.143 --> 00:42:11.105
The Golden Knights are losing
a whopping 12-0 in the second period.

784
00:42:11.189 --> 00:42:13.191
Your report is on every channel.

785
00:42:13.274 --> 00:42:15.860
Everybody's using your footage.
It's so cool.

786
00:42:15.944 --> 00:42:21.199
It's as if the magic in the sky
has put a spell on the Bruins' fortunes.

787
00:42:25.078 --> 00:42:27.247
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

788
00:42:31.209 --> 00:42:32.585
<b><font color="#ca004b">[WHIRRING]</font></b>

789
00:42:34.712 --> 00:42:36.339
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CLOCK CHIMING]</font></b>

790
00:42:39.801 --> 00:42:41.344
- Kid?
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>

791
00:42:42.679 --> 00:42:43.680
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BREATHING HEAVILY]</font></b>

792
00:42:48.059 --> 00:42:49.269
Agnes?

793
00:42:50.562 --> 00:42:53.648
Hiya, kid, can you see me okay?

794
00:42:53.731 --> 00:42:54.899
Whoa!

795
00:42:55.775 --> 00:42:57.402
What is this?

796
00:42:57.485 --> 00:43:00.113
What?
Haven't you ever heard of FaceTime?

797
00:43:00.196 --> 00:43:01.656
Oh, Agnes...

798
00:43:02.282 --> 00:43:04.367
Oh, I've missed you. Oh!

799
00:43:05.952 --> 00:43:07.620
It's so good to see you.

800
00:43:07.704 --> 00:43:10.582
Well, I wish I could say the same, kid,

801
00:43:10.665 --> 00:43:13.585
but word on the quad
is that Moira knows you're gone.

802
00:43:13.668 --> 00:43:17.213
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
- Yeah. And if she finds out

803
00:43:17.297 --> 00:43:20.758
that you're doing an assignment,
she'll go off her rocker.

804
00:43:21.050 --> 00:43:23.011
Oh, no. She loves her rocker.

805
00:43:23.094 --> 00:43:24.721
You need to come home.

806
00:43:25.138 --> 00:43:27.557
Well, I can't. I'm not done yet.

807
00:43:27.640 --> 00:43:29.267
Well, what's the holdup?

808
00:43:29.726 --> 00:43:30.727
Nothing.

809
00:43:31.978 --> 00:43:34.022
Mackenzie's not ten, for one thing.

810
00:43:34.105 --> 00:43:37.025
She's old, and she's got kids.

811
00:43:37.108 --> 00:43:40.695
And she says that
people run off with "piratis" instructors,

812
00:43:40.778 --> 00:43:42.447
which I think is how she says "pirates."

813
00:43:42.530 --> 00:43:46.659
And there's this prince named Hugh,
but she won't even consider him.

814
00:43:46.743 --> 00:43:48.870
She doesn't believe in happily ever after.

815
00:43:48.953 --> 00:43:50.497
Greta was right.

816
00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:52.248
- Sheesh!
- I know!

817
00:43:52.332 --> 00:43:55.168
Sounds like
she doesn't even believe in "happy."

818
00:43:56.669 --> 00:43:57.754
Agnes...

819
00:43:58.338 --> 00:43:59.631
I gotta go.

820
00:43:59.714 --> 00:44:01.883
I think I just figured out what to do.

821
00:44:01.966 --> 00:44:04.344
Well, okay, kid, but do it fast.

822
00:44:04.427 --> 00:44:07.096
You only have four days left.

823
00:44:07.180 --> 00:44:09.057
Right. Fast. Bye!

824
00:44:09.849 --> 00:44:12.227
Do I hang up? Or do you? Bye!

825
00:44:21.528 --> 00:44:22.946
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>

826
00:44:23.738 --> 00:44:26.699
Oh, good. You're awake, too.
I've got great news.

827
00:44:26.783 --> 00:44:29.953
I figured out why you're not interested
in happily ever after.

828
00:44:30.036 --> 00:44:31.746
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>
Because it's a fairy tale construct

829
00:44:31.830 --> 00:44:34.332
that teaches people
that normal life is not enough?

830
00:44:34.415 --> 00:44:36.543
Because you need a makeover!

831
00:44:37.752 --> 00:44:42.131
Relax. You've made it quite clear
that you prefer dressing like a crone.

832
00:44:42.799 --> 00:44:44.592
I'm talking about a happiness makeover.

833
00:44:44.676 --> 00:44:47.929
I hit the books last night,
and you know what you never see?

834
00:44:48.012 --> 00:44:49.848
A grumpy princess.

835
00:44:50.557 --> 00:44:51.558
Right.

836
00:44:51.641 --> 00:44:55.395
You need that moment
where you dance through the town

837
00:44:55.478 --> 00:44:58.982
and you're singing to the animals
and all the villagers.

838
00:44:59.065 --> 00:45:03.069
Huh. Yeah, okay. Remind me
to add frolicking to my schedule.

839
00:45:03.528 --> 00:45:06.447
You need to do something nice
for yourself for once.

840
00:45:06.531 --> 00:45:09.909
I can't today. I have to go to the bank,
help the kids with the homework,

841
00:45:09.993 --> 00:45:11.995
fix the light
that's broken in the bathroom.

842
00:45:12.078 --> 00:45:14.664
That is what Gary is for.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[LOUDLY]</font></b> Gary!

843
00:45:14.747 --> 00:45:16.249
Bathroom light!

844
00:45:16.332 --> 00:45:18.668
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> And, kids, homework!

845
00:45:18.751 --> 00:45:19.752
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERS]</font></b>

846
00:45:20.378 --> 00:45:23.006
Listen, Hugh told me
about this place downtown

847
00:45:23.089 --> 00:45:25.758
that is full of people,
places, and potions

848
00:45:25.842 --> 00:45:27.677
that are all designed to make you happy.

849
00:45:27.760 --> 00:45:29.846
There might even be someplace

850
00:45:29.929 --> 00:45:33.474
that could magically give you
the skin of a young maiden?

851
00:45:34.142 --> 00:45:35.143
Hmm?

852
00:45:36.102 --> 00:45:37.937
What about the kids?
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

853
00:45:38.021 --> 00:45:42.567
I'm a Fairy Godmother.
I think I can handle a couple of kids.

854
00:45:42.650 --> 00:45:44.652
I suppose I have to go grocery shopping,

855
00:45:44.736 --> 00:45:47.822
but just please don't let them
stare at a screen all day.

856
00:45:47.906 --> 00:45:48.907
Okay.

857
00:45:55.997 --> 00:45:57.081
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

858
00:46:07.300 --> 00:46:09.010
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHEERFUL MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

859
00:46:12.388 --> 00:46:13.389
Wow.

860
00:46:14.557 --> 00:46:15.975
So that's a-movie.

861
00:46:16.476 --> 00:46:18.269
What a wonderful a-movie.

862
00:46:25.443 --> 00:46:26.861
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SPEAKING LATIN]</font></b>

863
00:46:28.988 --> 00:46:30.823
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MIA EXCLAIMS, CHUCKLES]</font></b>

864
00:46:40.625 --> 00:46:41.626
Hello.

865
00:46:42.418 --> 00:46:43.670
Jane?

866
00:46:44.128 --> 00:46:45.880
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GIRL SINGING OVER LAPTOP]</font></b>
- Mia!

867
00:46:45.964 --> 00:46:47.090
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MIA GIGGLES]</font></b>

868
00:46:47.173 --> 00:46:48.258
Mia, stop!

869
00:46:50.426 --> 00:46:53.304
Son of a butterscotch.
That is good. Who is that?

870
00:46:53.388 --> 00:46:54.889
- Nobody.
- It's her.

871
00:46:54.973 --> 00:46:57.892
That's you? Oh, my goodness!

872
00:46:58.518 --> 00:47:00.562
Oh! You're really talented.

873
00:47:01.437 --> 00:47:02.814
You really think so?

874
00:47:02.897 --> 00:47:04.065
If I sounded like that,

875
00:47:04.148 --> 00:47:06.526
I would just walk around
singing to everyone.

876
00:47:06.609 --> 00:47:09.863
On the street, in school, in forests,

877
00:47:09.946 --> 00:47:13.032
in castles, on trains,
in dells and meadows,

878
00:47:13.116 --> 00:47:15.994
those large moving metal staircases!

879
00:47:16.077 --> 00:47:18.413
- Electronic superstores...
- <b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> Yeah, we get it.

880
00:47:18.496 --> 00:47:20.039
- You'd sing a lot.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[BOTH CHUCKLE]</font></b>

881
00:47:20.123 --> 00:47:21.166
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

882
00:47:21.249 --> 00:47:22.417
Oh, yeah.

883
00:47:22.500 --> 00:47:24.502
Well, you should put on a concert.

884
00:47:26.004 --> 00:47:27.547
