She can't.

885
00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:30.758
She freaks out
if she has to sing in front of people.

886
00:47:30.842 --> 00:47:31.885
Really? Why?

887
00:47:31.968 --> 00:47:34.095
It doesn't matter why.
I don't wanna talk about it.

888
00:47:41.102 --> 00:47:45.023
I'm afraid I'm not able
to make your mom or Jane happy.

889
00:47:45.106 --> 00:47:46.733
Mom doesn't believe in "happy,"

890
00:47:46.816 --> 00:47:49.402
or crafts or Christmas.

891
00:47:49.485 --> 00:47:50.653
I knew it!

892
00:47:50.737 --> 00:47:53.615
She says to Aunt Paula,
"There's no point in believing in happy,

893
00:47:53.698 --> 00:47:55.783
"because just when you do,
somethin' comes along

894
00:47:55.867 --> 00:47:58.453
"and smashes it
right off the side of I-95."

895
00:47:58.536 --> 00:47:59.746
What does she mean?

896
00:47:59.829 --> 00:48:02.081
I think she's talking about
when my dad died.

897
00:48:03.082 --> 00:48:04.209
He died?

898
00:48:06.252 --> 00:48:07.295
Oh, no!

899
00:48:07.962 --> 00:48:09.047
No, no, no.

900
00:48:09.881 --> 00:48:12.717
I thought he just ran off
to teach skinny pirates.

901
00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:15.428
Uh...

902
00:48:15.512 --> 00:48:19.641
He was in a car wreck about
four years ago, just before Christmas,

903
00:48:19.724 --> 00:48:22.936
but we don't really talk about him
because everybody gets upset.

904
00:48:25.146 --> 00:48:27.440
He used to sing with Jane all the time.

905
00:48:33.446 --> 00:48:34.614
Oh, dear!

906
00:48:41.162 --> 00:48:44.582
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]</font></b>
- Wow. Look at you. <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

907
00:48:46.709 --> 00:48:48.920
Mia, let's go get your sister.

908
00:48:49.003 --> 00:48:50.213
Okay!

909
00:48:52.340 --> 00:48:55.009
Thank you. Merry Christmas.
Have a nice day.

910
00:49:02.934 --> 00:49:04.978
<b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> We'll just do the same routine.

911
00:49:05.061 --> 00:49:07.146
We've got, like,
45 minutes left or something.

912
00:49:07.230 --> 00:49:10.066
Do your thing with the tea,
like you did last year. That was so good.

913
00:49:10.149 --> 00:49:11.985
And, yeah, we'll head off.

914
00:49:13.611 --> 00:49:14.779
Give me a sec.

915
00:49:20.618 --> 00:49:21.619
Mackenzie?

916
00:49:24.205 --> 00:49:25.290
Hugh?

917
00:49:27.041 --> 00:49:30.670
Why are you dressed like Prince Charming?

918
00:49:30.753 --> 00:49:32.797
It's not Prince Charming.

919
00:49:32.881 --> 00:49:34.632
Did Eleanor put you up to this?

920
00:49:34.716 --> 00:49:36.217
