921
00:49:36.301 --> 00:49:38.803
I, uh, like your hair, by the way.

922
00:49:39.596 --> 00:49:43.725
Today's the Boston Tea Party.
The Sons of Liberty never sleep.

923
00:49:43.808 --> 00:49:46.745
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]</font></b> You one of those weirdos
who dresses up for re-enactments?

924
00:49:46.769 --> 00:49:48.897
Samuel Adams. At your service.

925
00:49:49.439 --> 00:49:50.440
Oh.

926
00:49:51.191 --> 00:49:53.443
- Why?
- Civic duty, My Lady.

927
00:49:53.526 --> 00:49:55.862
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]</font></b>
Voting is a civic duty, but...

928
00:49:56.404 --> 00:49:57.989
Your trousers are very tight.

929
00:49:58.948 --> 00:50:01.242
<b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b>
Yeah.

930
00:50:01.326 --> 00:50:03.077
Hey, you wanna come check it out?

931
00:50:03.703 --> 00:50:05.705
- No.
- Come on, it'll be fun. Join us.

932
00:50:05.788 --> 00:50:08.541
Definitely not, but I'll see you Monday.

933
00:50:08.625 --> 00:50:09.834
You're missing out.

934
00:50:10.418 --> 00:50:13.671
The Sons of Liberty get pretty wild.

935
00:50:14.839 --> 00:50:17.175
Ain't no party like a Tea Party.

936
00:50:17.717 --> 00:50:18.968
Uh-huh.

937
00:50:19.802 --> 00:50:21.262
Oh, what am I doing?

938
00:50:21.346 --> 00:50:22.680
