1080
00:57:38.950 --> 00:57:41.661
- And the time before.
- I'm doing this.

1081
00:57:42.245 --> 00:57:44.080
Should be a fun ride to school.

1082
00:57:44.164 --> 00:57:45.665
<b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Okay. Come on. Chop, chop.

1083
00:57:45.999 --> 00:57:48.168
Really? Show choir?

1084
00:57:48.459 --> 00:57:50.461
How are you not moving your mouth?

1085
00:57:50.545 --> 00:57:51.880
I'm gonna kill you.

1086
00:57:51.963 --> 00:57:53.214
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CAR STARTS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Hmm?

1087
00:57:53.298 --> 00:57:54.591
Have fun!

1088
00:57:54.674 --> 00:57:55.925
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUFFLED]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Have fun!

1089
00:57:56.551 --> 00:57:59.846
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Maybe we just brush out your hair
before you see Hugh Prince.

1090
00:57:59.929 --> 00:58:00.972
Stop it!

1091
00:58:01.055 --> 00:58:02.724
He's very handsome,
and he's charming,

1092
00:58:02.807 --> 00:58:04.976
- and I just want you to look your best.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SHUSHES]</font></b>

1093
00:58:05.059 --> 00:58:06.227
Oh!

1094
00:58:06.311 --> 00:58:08.229
- Oh, there you are.
- Hi!

1095
00:58:08.313 --> 00:58:10.732
Got your go-bag.
We got our assignment.

1096
00:58:10.815 --> 00:58:12.358
Oh, give you one guess.

1097
00:58:12.442 --> 00:58:14.277
Exclusive access to the NATO Summit?

1098
00:58:14.360 --> 00:58:16.654
<b><font color="#cf685c">BOTH:</font></b> Nope! Storm Watch!

1099
00:58:16.738 --> 00:58:17.739
<b><font color="#ca004b">[VAN HONKS]</font></b>

1100
00:58:18.615 --> 00:58:19.616
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE GROANS]</font></b>

1101
00:58:20.825 --> 00:58:26.498
Oh, it's a carriage and a warrior?
Is it friendly? What are its powers?

1102
00:58:26.581 --> 00:58:27.832
Eh...

1103
00:58:27.957 --> 00:58:30.460
Four-wheel drive and studded snow tires.

1104
00:58:33.296 --> 00:58:34.923
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE AND ELEANOR GRUNTING]</font></b>

1105
00:58:36.508 --> 00:58:39.761
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">CHOIR:</font></b> The hills are alive

1106
00:58:39.844 --> 00:58:43.806
With the sound of music

1107
00:58:43.890 --> 00:58:46.142
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR VOCALIZING]</font></b>

1108
00:58:53.691 --> 00:58:54.859
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>

1109
00:58:55.693 --> 00:58:58.613
How does Storm Watch work exactly?

1110
00:58:58.696 --> 00:59:01.658
You see how delightful this is?
Everyone's happy and having fun?

1111
00:59:01.741 --> 00:59:03.660
Oh, it's perfect. So idyllic.

1112
00:59:03.743 --> 00:59:05.829
Well, we're gonna avoid
showing that at all costs.

1113
00:59:06.329 --> 00:59:09.833
Grant wants us to focus on traffic chaos
and runaway snowplows.

1114
00:59:09.916 --> 00:59:12.961
Or people fighting to the death
over canned food.

1115
00:59:13.044 --> 00:59:17.298
Mack won a bottle of champagne last year
for coming up with "Snow way, José,"

1116
00:59:17.382 --> 00:59:20.635
when the local Mexican restaurant
flooded from frozen pipes.

1117
00:59:20.718 --> 00:59:24.305
Most of our job is coming up with puns
like, "Snow laughing matter,"

1118
00:59:24.389 --> 00:59:26.099
or, "Snow end to the misery in sight."

1119
00:59:26.182 --> 00:59:28.476
"Snow way out."
"No business like snow business."

1120
00:59:28.560 --> 00:59:32.230
Unfortunately,
there's no, "Avalanche on Main Street,"

1121
00:59:32.313 --> 00:59:35.984
or, "Death by snowball," so I guess
we'll go with the old tried and true,

1122
00:59:36.067 --> 00:59:37.819
"Kids sledding on a hill" shot.

1123
00:59:37.902 --> 00:59:41.406
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CLAPPING]</font></b> Ooh!
Let's snow! That means, "Let's go."

1124
00:59:41.489 --> 00:59:44.367
That was it. You got it, Eleanor!
Do you wanna give me a hand?

1125
00:59:44.450 --> 00:59:46.077
Oh, no, thank you.

1126
00:59:48.329 --> 00:59:51.541
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CLOCK CHIMING]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Kid? Ya there? Whoo!

1127
00:59:52.083 --> 00:59:54.419
Are they keeping you in a dungeon?

1128
00:59:54.502 --> 00:59:56.671
No more fooling around.

1129
00:59:57.005 --> 01:00:00.091
Moira is about to
cough up her cocoa back here.

1130
01:00:00.466 --> 01:00:03.845
She's closing the portals
in two days' time.

1131
01:00:04.596 --> 01:00:06.431
<b><font color="#ca004b">[KIDS CHEERING]</font></b>

1132
01:00:10.226 --> 01:00:11.644
Is here okay?

1133
01:00:12.020 --> 01:00:13.622
- What do you think?
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Oh, uh...

1134
01:00:13.646 --> 01:00:16.649
Can he back up a little?
I'd love him to be closer to the action.

1135
01:00:16.733 --> 01:00:19.485
It looks so fun! Can we do it, too?

1136
01:00:19.569 --> 01:00:21.571
Uh, I can't.
I'm setting up for a live shot.

1137
01:00:21.654 --> 01:00:23.114
- <b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> This?
- Yeah. That's perfect.

1138
01:00:23.198 --> 01:00:24.365
- <b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> All right.
- Yes.

1139
01:00:24.991 --> 01:00:27.744
You know what? Actually,
there's a flying saucer in the trunk.

1140
01:00:27.827 --> 01:00:29.496
- Go have some fun.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>

1141
01:00:29.579 --> 01:00:31.122
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Okay, we're set here.

1142
01:00:48.431 --> 01:00:51.309
And we're live in three, two...

1143
01:00:52.310 --> 01:00:56.397
Good evening, everyone. I'm Hugh Prince
reporting from the town of Marblehead.

1144
01:00:56.481 --> 01:01:01.778
Now the blizzard means a flurry
of activity, and fun knows snow bounds.

1145
01:01:08.451 --> 01:01:09.452
Oh, no.

1146
01:01:09.536 --> 01:01:11.746
No, no, no, no. No.

1147
01:01:11.830 --> 01:01:12.831
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMING]</font></b>

1148
01:01:17.627 --> 01:01:19.462
The forecast calls
for a foot of snow tonight.

1149
01:01:19.546 --> 01:01:20.922
- Out of the way!
- But something

1150
01:01:21.005 --> 01:01:23.883
tells me the children of Marblehead
won't be chilling out.

1151
01:01:23.967 --> 01:01:26.803
They'll be laughing their sleds off!
Ahh!

1152
01:01:26.886 --> 01:01:29.472
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR CONTINUES SCREAMING]</font></b>

1153
01:01:32.809 --> 01:01:34.811
<b><font color="#ca004b">[REWINDING]</font></b>

1154
01:01:34.894 --> 01:01:37.146
They'll be laughing their sleds off!
Ahh!

1155
01:01:37.230 --> 01:01:39.524
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> This is why I never stop rolling.

1156
01:01:41.150 --> 01:01:45.572
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR AND MACKENZIE EXCLAIM]</font></b>
- That's a money shot right there.

1157
01:01:46.781 --> 01:01:50.076
I'm so sorry, Mackenzie.
I really messed up.

1158
01:01:50.160 --> 01:01:51.995
I really am very sorry.

1159
01:01:52.078 --> 01:01:54.455
Yeah, no, I'll tell her.

1160
01:01:55.832 --> 01:01:57.750
Yeah, yeah.
All right. All right.

1161
01:02:00.753 --> 01:02:02.714
Yeah, well, what you gonna do?

1162
01:02:02.797 --> 01:02:05.633
Okay. Thanks.
Talk to you tomorrow.

1163
01:02:06.426 --> 01:02:08.011
Are we fired?

1164
01:02:09.637 --> 01:02:13.224
The station's website
already has 200,000 hits.

1165
01:02:13.683 --> 01:02:17.854
Grant says we're viral like
his aunt's chicken pox. But he's thrilled.

1166
01:02:23.067 --> 01:02:24.652
We should celebrate!

1167
01:02:28.781 --> 01:02:29.782
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Wow.

1168
01:02:29.866 --> 01:02:31.534
That's one way.

1169
01:02:32.076 --> 01:02:34.204
I'll go get us more of this elixir.

1170
01:02:35.830 --> 01:02:38.208
- What is it called again?
- Lite beer.

1171
01:02:38.291 --> 01:02:39.292
Lite beer.

1172
01:02:39.375 --> 01:02:41.127
"LOL when the redhead wipes out."

1173
01:02:41.211 --> 01:02:44.005
"I hate that doofus reporter,
but loved it when he got slammed."

1174
01:02:44.088 --> 01:02:46.549
"Great seeing
those Channel 8 idiots get totaled."

1175
01:02:46.633 --> 01:02:49.427
Our clip has 400,000 hits and climbing.

1176
01:02:49.511 --> 01:02:50.512
Ouch!

1177
01:02:50.595 --> 01:02:52.889
Well, here's to going viral together.

1178
01:02:54.891 --> 01:02:57.060
For somebody
who takes himself so seriously,

1179
01:02:57.143 --> 01:02:59.395
you don't seem
that upset about going viral.

1180
01:02:59.479 --> 01:03:03.650
I knew it. You think
I'm boring and earnest, don't you?

1181
01:03:03.733 --> 01:03:06.194
No, of course not, Samuel Adams.

1182
01:03:06.277 --> 01:03:07.278
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCOFFS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1183
01:03:10.532 --> 01:03:12.408
Okay, that...
This is a game, too.

1184
01:03:12.784 --> 01:03:13.868
Ooh.

1185
01:03:13.952 --> 01:03:15.245
Good. Okay, that's cool.

1186
01:03:16.079 --> 01:03:17.664
This is a very big wand.

1187
01:03:18.414 --> 01:03:19.874
Pool cue. It's a pool cue.

1188
01:03:20.834 --> 01:03:23.211
That's what that is.
I get it. I see the mix-up.

1189
01:03:24.170 --> 01:03:25.171
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SNIFFS]</font></b>
Mmm.

1190
01:03:27.048 --> 01:03:29.175
Ooh, what is this perfect potion?

1191
01:03:29.259 --> 01:03:32.220
That's called a lemon drop.
And that is mine.

1192
01:03:33.471 --> 01:03:34.722
Was mine.

1193
01:03:36.391 --> 01:03:38.226
It really drops down.

1194
01:03:39.602 --> 01:03:41.020
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Yeah. Okay.

1195
01:03:41.104 --> 01:03:42.355
Did I win?

1196
01:03:43.314 --> 01:03:44.357
We're gettin' there.

1197
01:03:45.608 --> 01:03:46.609
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>
Oh!

1198
01:03:47.318 --> 01:03:50.238
Excuse me. Oh, no one's there.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1199
01:03:51.447 --> 01:03:53.992
I never pictured you as a divorced guy.

1200
01:03:54.075 --> 01:03:57.453
I know, it's impossible to think that
anyone would let all of this get away,

1201
01:03:57.537 --> 01:03:59.080
but it happened.

1202
01:03:59.164 --> 01:04:01.916
That's actually how I got
into the whole re-enactment stuff.

1203
01:04:02.000 --> 01:04:04.252
My son, he loves it,
and we do it on our weekends.

1204
01:04:04.377 --> 01:04:07.881
Oh. Now I feel terrible.
I didn't mean to call you a weirdo.

1205
01:04:07.964 --> 01:04:08.965
It's fine.

1206
01:04:09.048 --> 01:04:11.634
You know, one of the reasons
I wanted to come to Channel 8

1207
01:04:11.718 --> 01:04:13.678
was 'cause I used to
hear about this hotshot

1208
01:04:13.761 --> 01:04:16.389
that was getting her stories picked up
to the national level.

1209
01:04:16.472 --> 01:04:18.933
I mean, I'm surprised
you're not running the joint.

1210
01:04:19.475 --> 01:04:23.521
Actually, they did offer me the job,
but it was too soon after...

1211
01:04:24.230 --> 01:04:26.858
Yeah, Duff told me
about your husband. I'm...

1212
01:04:26.941 --> 01:04:28.943
Right, so I needed to focus on my girls,

1213
01:04:29.027 --> 01:04:31.988
and they gave the job to Grant,
and here we are.

1214
01:04:33.072 --> 01:04:34.282
I'm sorry, Mack.

1215
01:04:34.657 --> 01:04:36.743
I'm sorry, too.
Grant is an abomination.

1216
01:04:36.826 --> 01:04:38.119
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1217
01:04:39.496 --> 01:04:41.998
What about you?
What's it like being divorced?

1218
01:04:42.081 --> 01:04:45.543
Oh, it's... What can I say?
<b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b> It's lonely.

1219
01:04:45.627 --> 01:04:47.587
Mmm, yeah, I get that.

1220
01:04:48.588 --> 01:04:51.716
Sometimes, you just want somebody to,
you know, come over and...

1221
01:04:53.218 --> 01:04:54.636
Shovel the driveway.

1222
01:04:56.930 --> 01:04:59.766
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>
To shoveling the driveway.

1223
01:04:59.849 --> 01:05:01.559
Shoveling the driveway.

1224
01:05:03.311 --> 01:05:06.147
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Okay, I'll tell you what.
We'll line up a shot for you.

1225
01:05:06.231 --> 01:05:07.232
You've got this.

1226
01:05:07.315 --> 01:05:10.944
With your wand, the tip of it,
you hit the white one, hit the red one

1227
01:05:11.027 --> 01:05:13.363
to go right into this pocket.
It's called a pocket.

1228
01:05:13.446 --> 01:05:14.906
- Got it.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Ready?

1229
01:05:14.989 --> 01:05:16.324
White, red, pocket.

1230
01:05:16.741 --> 01:05:17.951
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b>

1231
01:05:18.034 --> 01:05:19.035
Ooh.

1232
01:05:19.118 --> 01:05:21.329
Mother of fudge! Are you okay?

1233
01:05:21.704 --> 01:05:24.749
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANING]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> Did I win? I think I won.

1234
01:05:26.793 --> 01:05:29.295
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR CHANTING IN LATIN]</font></b>

1235
01:05:32.006 --> 01:05:33.550
Oh, wow!

1236
01:05:33.633 --> 01:05:35.009
<b><font color="#ca004b">[IN ENGLISH]</font></b>
I know, right?

1237
01:05:35.385 --> 01:05:38.137
It took me a whole month
to learn that spell.

1238
01:05:38.596 --> 01:05:40.014
But it was worth it.

1239
01:05:44.435 --> 01:05:46.563
- You might be right about Hugh.
- Oh!

1240
01:05:46.646 --> 01:05:51.693
I'm not saying he's my prince,
but he's kinda charming.

1241
01:05:51.776 --> 01:05:54.821
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLING]</font></b> I knew it. He's handsome...
- Eleanor.

1242
01:05:54.904 --> 01:05:57.866
I know you wanna help, but...

1243
01:05:58.992 --> 01:06:01.870
I'm not quite sure
I'm ready for another fairy tale.

1244
01:06:18.178 --> 01:06:20.221
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Eleanor, on the other hand,

1245
01:06:20.305 --> 01:06:23.224
had spent her life
believing in fairy tales.

1246
01:06:23.308 --> 01:06:26.978
Little did she know,
this one was about to come to an end.

1247
01:06:27.061 --> 01:06:29.189
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[OPERA MUSIC PLAYING ON RECORDER]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[HUMMING]</font></b>

1248
01:06:33.610 --> 01:06:35.278
<b><font color="#ca004b">[PANTING]</font></b>
Oh!

1249
01:06:39.282 --> 01:06:40.450
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUSIC STOPS]</font></b>

1250
01:06:40.533 --> 01:06:43.912
<b><font color="#ca004b">[PANTING]</font></b> I'm not going
to ask you where Eleanor is.

1251
01:06:44.412 --> 01:06:46.122
Because I know you won't tell me.

1252
01:06:46.206 --> 01:06:48.583
Even if I did know, I wouldn't tell you.

1253
01:06:48.666 --> 01:06:49.876
That's what I just said!

1254
01:06:49.959 --> 01:06:53.254
Good! I'm glad
we're finally seeing eye to eye.

1255
01:06:53.338 --> 01:06:55.632
Oh, Agnes, listen to me.

1256
01:06:55.715 --> 01:07:00.762
I don't know exactly what she's up to,
but Eleanor is not going to save us.

1257
01:07:00.845 --> 01:07:02.347
No one can.

1258
01:07:02.972 --> 01:07:07.101
At midnight tomorrow, the Motherland
will close its doors for good.

1259
01:07:07.185 --> 01:07:10.730
- Oh, that's a real shame!
- But that's not all.

1260
01:07:10.813 --> 01:07:15.068
If Eleanor is not here,
she will be stripped of her magic.

1261
01:07:15.151 --> 01:07:17.278
- Disenchantment?
- Yes!

1262
01:07:17.904 --> 01:07:21.741
In all my years here,
I have never lost a student.

1263
01:07:21.825 --> 01:07:24.410
And I am not about to lose one now!

1264
01:07:24.494 --> 01:07:28.248
Even if I have to take drastic measures.

1265
01:07:28.331 --> 01:07:29.541
So,

1266
01:07:31.084 --> 01:07:37.006
if someone who loves Eleanor
happens to know where she is,

1267
01:07:37.090 --> 01:07:42.178
now would be a good time to tell her
to get her fairy tail back here!

1268
01:07:43.012 --> 01:07:45.014
I'm gonna go make a call

1269
01:07:45.098 --> 01:07:48.101
that's not at all related
to this conversation.

1270
01:07:48.184 --> 01:07:50.395
Ah. Hmm.

1271
01:07:50.520 --> 01:07:52.939
<b><font color="#cf685c">GRANT:</font></b> Are you kidding me? Oh, my God!

1272
01:07:53.022 --> 01:07:55.608
Ladies and gentlemen,
we did it! Fourth place!

1273
01:07:55.692 --> 01:07:57.253
- Hope to see you there.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[STAFF CHEERING]</font></b>

1274
01:07:57.277 --> 01:07:58.987
- We've reached the top...
- See you later.

1275
01:07:59.070 --> 01:08:01.781
- <b><font color="#cf685c">GRANT:</font></b> Fourth place!
- Mackenzie. Hi!

1276
01:08:01.865 --> 01:08:04.909
The other donut-eaters just told me
the most amazing thing ever.

1277
01:08:04.993 --> 01:08:06.911
- Brace yourself, because it's big.
- Mmm-hmm.

1278
01:08:06.995 --> 01:08:09.455
There's a holiday party tonight.
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

1279
01:08:09.539 --> 01:08:12.667
I know all about the holiday party,
and I'm not going. It's not my thing.

1280
01:08:12.750 --> 01:08:16.504
- What part? Parties? Christmas? Fun?
- Mmm. Uh-huh.

1281
01:08:16.588 --> 01:08:19.424
Fine, stay home. After all,
nine out of ten fairy tales begin with,

1282
01:08:19.507 --> 01:08:21.467
"Once upon a time,
something amazing happened

1283
01:08:21.551 --> 01:08:23.928
"while she was drinking wine
in her sweatpants."

1284
01:08:25.638 --> 01:08:26.973
Think about it.

1285
01:08:27.056 --> 01:08:28.933
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHRISTMAS CAROL PLAYING]</font></b>

1286
01:08:35.648 --> 01:08:38.318
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING OUT OF TUNE]</font></b>
Joy to the world

1287
01:08:38.401 --> 01:08:40.862
Joy to the world

1288
01:08:40.945 --> 01:08:43.364
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SNORTS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> I know, buddy. My ears hurt too.

1289
01:08:45.241 --> 01:08:47.368
- Oh, wow!
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL GASP]</font></b>

1290
01:08:47.452 --> 01:08:48.495
<b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> Pretty.

1291
01:08:49.829 --> 01:08:53.374
You look so pretty.
Eleanor, you did a great job.

1292
01:08:53.458 --> 01:08:55.251
I didn't do that. That was all her.

1293
01:08:55.335 --> 01:08:59.047
Really? You can make yourself
look like that without any magic?

1294
01:08:59.130 --> 01:09:00.131
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Mm-hmm.

1295
01:09:00.215 --> 01:09:03.301
Yes, because she's beautiful
inside and out.

1296
01:09:03.384 --> 01:09:04.928
Aw, true.

1297
01:09:05.178 --> 01:09:07.972
And she's wearing
the only thing that really matters.

1298
01:09:08.056 --> 01:09:09.599
- Pushup bra?
- Spanx?

1299
01:09:09.682 --> 01:09:10.850
<b><font color="#ca004b">[LAUGHING]</font></b>

1300
01:09:10.934 --> 01:09:13.311
- A smile.
- Uh, actually, all three.

1301
01:09:13.937 --> 01:09:15.230
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL CHUCKLE]</font></b>

1302
01:09:16.147 --> 01:09:18.399
Are you feeling okay about tomorrow?

1303
01:09:18.483 --> 01:09:21.069
- Yeah, I think so.
- Okay. Good.

1304
01:09:23.029 --> 01:09:25.365
Look at us.
We're both outside our comfort zone.

1305
01:09:25.990 --> 01:09:27.176
- Yeah. Okay.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CLOCK CHIMING]</font></b>

1306
01:09:27.200 --> 01:09:31.162
- What's that sound?
- Oh, that's probably Agnes FaceTiming.

1307
01:09:31.246 --> 01:09:32.831
I should grab that.

1308
01:09:32.914 --> 01:09:35.750
Disenchanted? Forever?

1309
01:09:35.834 --> 01:09:38.127
I'm sorry, kid, but it's over.

1310
01:09:38.211 --> 01:09:40.296
No, I won't give up.

1311
01:09:40.672 --> 01:09:43.466
They just need to see
one happily ever after.

1312
01:09:43.550 --> 01:09:47.136
I can get her there. I know it.
I just need to speed things up.

1313
01:09:47.220 --> 01:09:51.266
Well, you better make it very speedy,
'cause if you don't get back in time,

1314
01:09:51.349 --> 01:09:55.770
forget being a Fairy Godmother,
you won't be a Fairy anything.

1315
01:09:55.854 --> 01:09:59.732
At midnight tomorrow,
they're closing the Motherland for good!

1316
01:09:59.816 --> 01:10:01.109
Oh, I need to go.

1317
01:10:01.651 --> 01:10:03.236
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCRATCHING]</font></b>

1318
01:10:05.280 --> 01:10:07.657
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[DISCO MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>
- Fourth place! Fourth place!

1319
01:10:07.740 --> 01:10:10.869
Fourth place, baby! Fourth place!

1320
01:10:15.582 --> 01:10:16.875
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUSIC CONTINUES]</font></b>

1321
01:10:25.550 --> 01:10:27.177
<b><font color="#cf685c">BARB:</font></b> It was a crazy night.

1322
01:10:27.260 --> 01:10:28.761
Oh, he took me home, and let me...

1323
01:10:28.845 --> 01:10:31.222
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> I was hoping
this would go somewhere else.

1324
01:10:31.764 --> 01:10:33.224
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INAUDIBLE]</font></b>

1325
01:10:34.142 --> 01:10:37.645
<b><font color="#cf685c">DUFF:</font></b> What a story. Typical Barb.

1326
01:10:37.729 --> 01:10:40.190
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> A glittery gown
turns a frown upside down.

1327
01:10:40.273 --> 01:10:43.193
A glittery gown turns a frown upside down.

1328
01:10:43.943 --> 01:10:46.905
Yeah. A glittery gown
turns a frown upside down.

1329
01:10:46.988 --> 01:10:52.327
I was sweating so bad that my dress
was basically see-through. You remember?

1330
01:10:52.410 --> 01:10:55.622
And I had streaks of self-tanner
just running down,

1331
01:10:55.705 --> 01:10:58.917
and I looked like a zebra
in a wet T-shirt contest.

1332
01:11:00.293 --> 01:11:02.712
That's why I don't wear white
on the air anymore.

1333
01:11:02.795 --> 01:11:04.964
Well, I'm all out of war stories.

1334
01:11:05.840 --> 01:11:07.342
How 'bout a dance?

1335
01:11:08.676 --> 01:11:09.761
<b><font color="#ca004b">[UPBEAT POP MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

1336
01:11:43.711 --> 01:11:46.089
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

1337
01:12:23.168 --> 01:12:24.711
<b><font color="#ca004b">[POP SONG RESUMES PLAYING]</font></b>

1338
01:12:24.794 --> 01:12:25.962
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

1339
01:12:31.342 --> 01:12:32.385
<b><font color="#cf685c">HUGH:</font></b> Mack! Mack!

1340
01:12:37.098 --> 01:12:38.641
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANS]</font></b>

1341
01:12:41.144 --> 01:12:45.106
Mackenzie?
Are you in there? Mackenzie?

1342
01:12:45.190 --> 01:12:46.482
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Eleanor?

1343
01:12:46.566 --> 01:12:49.277
- What are you doing here?
- Nothing.

1344
01:12:49.360 --> 01:12:54.324
Something really strange happened to me
on the dance floor... Oh, of course.

1345
01:12:54.407 --> 01:12:55.408
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MUTTERING]</font></b>

1346
01:12:55.492 --> 01:12:58.036
You had something to do
with this, didn't you?

1347
01:12:58.119 --> 01:13:00.079
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMING]</font></b>
What the heck?

1348
01:13:01.998 --> 01:13:04.334
Eleanor! Eleanor!

1349
01:13:05.293 --> 01:13:06.461
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE YELPS]</font></b>

1350
01:13:09.297 --> 01:13:10.298
Oh, wow!

1351
01:13:11.090 --> 01:13:12.133
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

1352
01:13:13.009 --> 01:13:14.761
Nice dress. Is it new?

1353
01:13:14.844 --> 01:13:16.888
What have you done to me?

1354
01:13:16.971 --> 01:13:20.642
- Don't be mad. I'm just trying to help.
- Really? Like this?

1355
01:13:20.725 --> 01:13:22.310
You look absolutely beautiful...

1356
01:13:24.771 --> 01:13:29.317
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[LAUGHING]</font></b> What happened to you?
- Hi, Barb, I just... <b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b>

1357
01:13:30.068 --> 01:13:33.404
I ripped my dress, so I borrowed this
from the wardrobe department.

1358
01:13:33.488 --> 01:13:35.323
- It's hilarious.
- Yeah.

1359
01:13:35.406 --> 01:13:38.660
You know, my kid has a costume
just like that at home. <b><font color="#ca004b">[SNICKERS]</font></b>

1360
01:13:39.953 --> 01:13:41.120
Treat it as a costume.

1361
01:13:41.204 --> 01:13:42.205
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MACKENZIE GROWLS]</font></b>

1362
01:13:42.288 --> 01:13:45.124
Don't be mad.
Don't be mad! Mackenzie!

1363
01:13:46.709 --> 01:13:49.087
Mackenzie! Where are you going?

1364
01:13:49.170 --> 01:13:52.632
Home. Before anybody else sees me.

1365
01:13:52.715 --> 01:13:56.094
What? No! Look at you!

1366
01:13:56.177 --> 01:13:57.595
You look like a princess.

1367
01:13:57.679 --> 01:14:00.098
<b><font color="#ca004b">[OVER SPEAKERS]</font></b>
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> And you're at a ball. Sort of.

1368
01:14:00.181 --> 01:14:02.308
And Duff
and all the other peasants are here.

1369
01:14:02.392 --> 01:14:06.229
And you even waltzed with
the most handsome of all the princes.

1370
01:14:06.312 --> 01:14:09.274
- Hugh Prince!
- Oh, I knew it was you.

1371
01:14:09.357 --> 01:14:12.360
And you said it at the hotel.
You think he's charming.

1372
01:14:12.443 --> 01:14:13.987
And now he's noticing you.

1373
01:14:14.070 --> 01:14:17.073
Isn't that what you wanted
since you were ten years old?

1374
01:14:17.156 --> 01:14:21.995
So, why fight true love when you can
just kiss and live happily ever after?

1375
01:14:22.078 --> 01:14:23.079
Because...

1376
01:14:26.374 --> 01:14:27.375
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1377
01:14:27.917 --> 01:14:32.130
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b> Happily ever after?
- Yes!

1378
01:14:32.547 --> 01:14:34.757
You're her prince.
Now, let's get this done.

1379
01:14:34.841 --> 01:14:38.178
- No! Eleanor, this isn't what I want.
- I... Why are you...

1380
01:14:38.845 --> 01:14:41.055
Wait a minute, wait a minute.
You're that...

1381
01:14:42.015 --> 01:14:44.517
- You're flying saucer chick.
- Yes. That's me.

1382
01:14:44.601 --> 01:14:45.602
Hey.

1383
01:14:45.685 --> 01:14:48.021
Oh, Mackenzie and Hugh
said we were a big hit.

1384
01:14:48.521 --> 01:14:49.856
Is that so?

1385
01:14:49.939 --> 01:14:52.567
Oh, yes, they were so worried
about getting fired.

1386
01:14:52.650 --> 01:14:56.529
But I guess all you need
for job security is a viral video.

1387
01:14:56.613 --> 01:14:58.281
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL GASPING]</font></b>

1388
01:14:58.948 --> 01:15:02.160
- No, it's not like that.
- That is not exactly what...

1389
01:15:02.243 --> 01:15:07.540
9:00 a.m., my office, tomorrow morning.
We can talk about job security then. Mmm?

1390
01:15:16.174 --> 01:15:20.803
Mackenzie! Mackenzie, I'm sorry.
Please just talk to me.

1391
01:15:20.887 --> 01:15:23.932
Why should I talk to you?
You don't listen to anything I say.

1392
01:15:24.015 --> 01:15:25.767
- That's not true.
- It is.

1393
01:15:25.850 --> 01:15:28.478
You came here and did exactly
what you promised you wouldn't do.

1394
01:15:28.561 --> 01:15:31.105
And the worst part is,
you didn't even need to.

1395
01:15:31.189 --> 01:15:34.859
I was actually having fun tonight.
I felt pretty.

1396
01:15:34.943 --> 01:15:36.486
But why isn't that enough for you?

1397
01:15:36.986 --> 01:15:41.157
Why am I a failure
unless I'm dressed like ginger Elvis?

1398
01:15:41.241 --> 01:15:44.619
- You're not a failure.
- Then why are you here?

1399
01:15:44.702 --> 01:15:48.540
Because I don't wanna fail!
They're closing down the Motherland.

1400
01:15:48.998 --> 01:15:51.876
So, you're my only chance
at being a Fairy Godmother.

1401
01:15:52.627 --> 01:15:55.547
And if I don't get you
to "happily ever after,"

1402
01:15:55.630 --> 01:15:59.843
then I'll have to spend
the rest of my life as a Tooth Fairy.

1403
01:15:59.926 --> 01:16:04.389
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCOFFS]</font></b> This is all about you.
- No! Of course not. I...

1404
01:16:05.640 --> 01:16:07.141
Wait. Is it?

1405
01:16:07.559 --> 01:16:11.312
All this time, I thought you cared
about wanting to make me happy.

1406
01:16:11.396 --> 01:16:12.814
You just want it for you.

1407
01:16:12.897 --> 01:16:15.400
You don't care what I want,
not if it gets in your way.

1408
01:16:16.276 --> 01:16:18.528
I'm so sorry, Mackenzie.

1409
01:16:18.611 --> 01:16:21.489
I'm sorry too, Eleanor,
but you need to leave.

1410
01:16:29.706 --> 01:16:30.707
Mackenzie!

1411
01:16:32.834 --> 01:16:36.504
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> She was right about everything.
I'm not Fairy Godmother material.

1412
01:16:36.588 --> 01:16:40.341
And "happily ever afters,"
those are just for fairy tales.

1413
01:16:40.425 --> 01:16:41.759
But you helped us.

1414
01:16:43.761 --> 01:16:46.598
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MIA:</font></b> Don't go.
- I'm sorry. It's over.

1415
01:16:46.681 --> 01:16:48.892
- She'll calm down.
- But we need you.

1416
01:16:49.309 --> 01:16:50.393
I have to go.

1417
01:16:51.686 --> 01:16:52.896
Goodbye, girls.

1418
01:17:05.492 --> 01:17:06.618
Bye, Bingo.

1419
01:17:08.328 --> 01:17:09.537
Bingo?

1420
01:17:12.207 --> 01:17:13.708
Who's that pig?

1421
01:17:18.880 --> 01:17:20.340
Now we have a pig and a dog.

1422
01:17:23.384 --> 01:17:25.929
Eleanor, where are you?
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SHUDDERS]</font></b>

1423
01:17:35.188 --> 01:17:38.525
Gourds? Pumpkins? Carriages?

1424
01:17:38.608 --> 01:17:40.151
Transport.

1425
01:17:41.611 --> 01:17:42.612
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

1426
01:17:52.789 --> 01:17:53.790
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b>

1427
01:18:04.425 --> 01:18:05.593
Hi.

1428
01:18:05.677 --> 01:18:08.221
- I need to tell you something.
- I just wanna...

1429
01:18:08.304 --> 01:18:09.305
Yes.

1430
01:18:09.514 --> 01:18:12.267
I really wanted to apologize
about last night.

1431
01:18:12.350 --> 01:18:13.935
I'm just completely mortified.

1432
01:18:14.018 --> 01:18:18.439
I think I had too much punch or something,
and things got a little wild.

1433
01:18:18.523 --> 01:18:21.359
No, it's... I mean, yeah,
I was surprised, but...

1434
01:18:22.569 --> 01:18:23.778
But not in a bad way.

1435
01:18:24.445 --> 01:18:25.780
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BOTH CHUCKLE]</font></b>

1436
01:18:26.906 --> 01:18:31.035
Hey! You two!
What are you doin'? Get in here!

1437
01:18:32.328 --> 01:18:34.622
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GROANING]</font></b>
My tum-tum.

1438
01:18:35.373 --> 01:18:39.252
I'm gonna be straight with you guys.
I hit the eggnog way too hard last night.

1439
01:18:39.335 --> 01:18:42.672
So, I'm gonna keep this quick.
Did you fake the flying saucer story?

1440
01:18:43.173 --> 01:18:45.550
- No! We would never fake a story.
- Absolutely not.

1441
01:18:45.633 --> 01:18:48.261
Really?
Then how do you explain this?

1442
01:18:49.929 --> 01:18:50.930
Huh?

1443
01:18:52.182 --> 01:18:56.144
And why is flying saucer girl
at the Bruins game?

1444
01:18:56.686 --> 01:19:00.440
'Cause she's my cousin,
and she's visiting from Canada.

1445
01:19:00.523 --> 01:19:02.859
You seriously want me to believe
that you and your cousin

1446
01:19:02.942 --> 01:19:05.403
had nothing to do with the fireballs?

1447
01:19:05.904 --> 01:19:06.988
It was an accident.

1448
01:19:07.071 --> 01:19:09.782
Ah! So was the blackout too, I suppose.

1449
01:19:10.200 --> 01:19:11.409
That's her, isn't it?

1450
01:19:12.243 --> 01:19:15.663
We had three big news stories this week,

1451
01:19:15.747 --> 01:19:19.959
and your cousin was there
for every single one of them. Yes or no?

1452
01:19:20.043 --> 01:19:21.711
Mack, what's goin' on?

1453
01:19:21.794 --> 01:19:23.338
I just... I can't.

1454
01:19:23.421 --> 01:19:27.383
It's really hard to explain.
But I did not fake a story.

1455
01:19:28.510 --> 01:19:32.972
Yeah. You lack the initiative
to pull that off. I actually believe you.

1456
01:19:33.056 --> 01:19:35.558
Plus, your cousin seems crazy.
She is, right?

1457
01:19:35.642 --> 01:19:39.395
No! No, she's just a little different.

1458
01:19:39.479 --> 01:19:44.651
She's a chaos machine.
And you should be ashamed of yourself...

1459
01:19:48.863 --> 01:19:50.740
For not cutting me in sooner.

1460
01:19:50.823 --> 01:19:53.409
You're good. She is ratings gold.

1461
01:19:53.493 --> 01:19:55.829
Here's what we'll do.
We're gonna put a camera on her,

1462
01:19:55.912 --> 01:19:59.541
and we are gonna let her fly
her freak flag until we're number one.

1463
01:19:59.624 --> 01:20:02.001
- That's exploitation. No.
- But that's not news.

1464
01:20:02.085 --> 01:20:04.295
I know. It's gonna be awesome.

1465
01:20:06.714 --> 01:20:07.757
No!

1466
01:20:07.841 --> 01:20:10.885
I won't let you
take somebody kind and good

1467
01:20:10.969 --> 01:20:12.637
and turn them into a sideshow.

1468
01:20:12.720 --> 01:20:16.307
You're a single mom, and you haven't put
a good story out in I don't know how long,

1469
01:20:16.391 --> 01:20:19.060
so "no" isn't really an option for you.

1470
01:20:19.143 --> 01:20:21.604
You do what I say, or you're fired.

1471
01:20:25.275 --> 01:20:28.319
- I am done doing things your way.
- Mack, I'm not sure you...

1472
01:20:28.403 --> 01:20:30.321
You're the reason we're in last place.

1473
01:20:30.405 --> 01:20:32.407
Ah! Fourth place.

1474
01:20:32.490 --> 01:20:34.742
You want us to spin things
and twist things

1475
01:20:34.826 --> 01:20:37.537
and tell stories about bad people
doing bad things,

1476
01:20:37.620 --> 01:20:39.706
but people want more than fearmongering.

1477
01:20:39.789 --> 01:20:41.124
They wanna...

1478
01:20:41.207 --> 01:20:45.753
To laugh, and to hope, and be inspired
to see the magic in the world.

1479
01:20:45.837 --> 01:20:47.964
- 'Cause it's real.
- That's cute.

1480
01:20:48.590 --> 01:20:49.674
You're fired.

1481
01:20:49.757 --> 01:20:51.259
Yeah. No kidding.

1482
01:20:52.552 --> 01:20:54.679
You deserve so much better
than this place.

1483
01:20:54.762 --> 01:20:57.056
I know. That's what I was tryin'
to tell you before.

1484
01:20:57.140 --> 01:20:59.100
I took the job at Channel 4, so...

1485
01:20:59.767 --> 01:21:02.145
<b><font color="#ca004b">[INHALES]</font></b>
Merry Christmas. I quit.

1486
01:21:03.855 --> 01:21:05.190
How's that for spectacle?

1487
01:21:16.493 --> 01:21:18.495
- Bye.
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CELL PHONE RINGING]</font></b>

1488
01:21:21.039 --> 01:21:24.209
Hello? Yes, this is Mackenzie.

1489
01:21:25.418 --> 01:21:27.128
Oh, hi, Mr. Clancy.

1490
01:21:29.047 --> 01:21:30.507
Wait, Jane what?

1491
01:21:33.176 --> 01:21:36.429
Jane? Jane, sweetie!

1492
01:21:38.515 --> 01:21:39.599
Jane?

1493
01:21:42.268 --> 01:21:44.979
Jane? Jane!

1494
01:21:45.897 --> 01:21:47.315
<b><font color="#ca004b">[PANTING]</font></b>

1495
01:21:53.613 --> 01:21:54.614
Oh!

1496
01:22:10.588 --> 01:22:12.841
<b><font color="#ca004b">[DOOR OPENING]</font></b>

1497
01:22:14.050 --> 01:22:17.595
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Janie? Honey?
- No, go away.

1498
01:22:19.097 --> 01:22:20.181
Uh...

1499
01:22:20.265 --> 01:22:24.394
Mr. Clancy called. Honey, you're supposed
to be on stage for the rehearsal.

1500
01:22:30.942 --> 01:22:32.443
Is that Dad's guitar?

1501
01:22:34.737 --> 01:22:38.658
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CRYING]</font></b>
You were right. You were right.

1502
01:22:40.160 --> 01:22:43.079
I can't do this.
I can't do anything.

1503
01:22:43.621 --> 01:22:45.206
Oh, I never said that.

1504
01:22:45.290 --> 01:22:47.584
Yeah, well, you never said that I could.

1505
01:22:49.294 --> 01:22:52.463
Or that you thought that I'd be amazing.

1506
01:22:54.215 --> 01:22:57.010
But Eleanor did.

1507
01:22:59.053 --> 01:23:04.309
And now she's gone.
And I can't do this. I can't...

1508
01:23:11.733 --> 01:23:13.484
I'm so sorry.

1509
01:23:17.322 --> 01:23:22.076
Honey, if you need Eleanor,
I'll find her. I promise.

1510
01:23:26.331 --> 01:23:28.917
Should we bring Dad's guitar with us
for good luck?

1511
01:23:32.295 --> 01:23:34.589
Gary, we need you!

1512
01:23:34.672 --> 01:23:37.091
- <b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> He's not here!
- Where's Eleanor?

1513
01:23:37.175 --> 01:23:40.720
Gary, I'll leave the lids
off the trash cans if you just come out!

1514
01:23:41.095 --> 01:23:42.889
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> We need you!
<b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> Eleanor!

1515
01:23:42.972 --> 01:23:44.974
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMING]</font></b> <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Gary!

1516
01:23:45.725 --> 01:23:49.562
I'm not sure he can actually
understand human. But look!

1517
01:23:49.646 --> 01:23:52.023
I think Aunt Paula's
been looking for Eleanor.

1518
01:24:23.137 --> 01:24:24.138
- Ooh!
- <b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Ah.

1519
01:24:26.349 --> 01:24:27.684
It's hopeless.

1520
01:24:27.767 --> 01:24:32.021
<b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Are you sure a pumpkin carriage
is the fastest way back to the Motherland?

1521
01:24:32.105 --> 01:24:33.189
Yes, but...

1522
01:24:33.273 --> 01:24:36.109
- I'm never going to get it.
- No worries.

1523
01:24:37.318 --> 01:24:39.028
That was our last pumpkin.

1524
01:24:40.780 --> 01:24:42.073
I've got an idea.

1525
01:24:46.744 --> 01:24:47.745
Ta-da!

1526
01:24:48.079 --> 01:24:49.497
That's not a pumpkin.

1527
01:24:51.332 --> 01:24:53.751
- No. I know it's not a pumpkin.
- Good.

1528
01:24:53.835 --> 01:24:57.255
- Okay. You know what? Loosen up, right?
- All right.

1529
01:24:57.338 --> 01:25:00.550
You know, just really stay loose
and don't think about the fact

1530
01:25:00.633 --> 01:25:02.427
that that's a watermelon,
not a pumpkin,

1531
01:25:02.510 --> 01:25:05.138
and you might not have
enough magic left to get home,

1532
01:25:05.221 --> 01:25:06.764
and you might be stuck here forever.

1533
01:25:08.433 --> 01:25:10.768
I'm sorry, that wasn't
a very good pep talk.

1534
01:25:10.852 --> 01:25:12.854
No. All right.

1535
01:25:12.937 --> 01:25:15.940
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CHANTING IN LATIN]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Eleanor! Paula!

1536
01:25:16.024 --> 01:25:17.025
Hi!

1537
01:25:19.944 --> 01:25:20.945
<b><font color="#cf685c">MIA:</font></b> Whoa!

1538
01:25:21.613 --> 01:25:22.697
What happened?

1539
01:25:23.448 --> 01:25:25.700
Oh, we were trying to make a carriage.

1540
01:25:26.868 --> 01:25:28.028
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SOFTLY]</font></b>
It's not going well.

1541
01:25:28.453 --> 01:25:31.664
Jane, why are you here?
Why aren't you at the parade?

1542
01:25:32.081 --> 01:25:33.750
I can't do this without you.

1543
01:25:36.336 --> 01:25:38.588
Please, Eleanor. I'm so sorry.

1544
01:25:40.215 --> 01:25:41.341
Janie needs you.

1545
01:25:44.177 --> 01:25:45.637
We need you.

1546
01:25:50.225 --> 01:25:51.226
Okay.

1547
01:25:53.645 --> 01:25:56.397
First things first.
Let's get you dressed.

1548
01:26:08.910 --> 01:26:09.911
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1549
01:26:09.994 --> 01:26:12.747
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> Son of a butterscotch!
I actually did it!

1550
01:26:12.831 --> 01:26:14.707
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL CHUCKLE]</font></b>

1551
01:26:14.791 --> 01:26:17.210
- You look amazing.
- You really do.

1552
01:26:18.336 --> 01:26:20.839
Perfect outfit, check. Now what?

1553
01:26:20.964 --> 01:26:21.965
Um...

1554
01:26:22.048 --> 01:26:25.802
Oh, we need to get there. I'm supposed
to be on stage in 20 minutes.

1555
01:26:25.885 --> 01:26:28.346
But the parade is all the way downtown.
There's no way.

1556
01:26:28.429 --> 01:26:31.015
Actually, there is.

1557
01:26:31.474 --> 01:26:33.852
Eleanor, no.
You need that to get home.

1558
01:26:33.935 --> 01:26:36.271
Not as much as I need to do this.

1559
01:26:36.354 --> 01:26:38.773
All right, everyone, step back.
Go, go!

1560
01:26:41.860 --> 01:26:44.654
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHANTING IN LATIN]</font></b>

1561
01:27:17.604 --> 01:27:19.272
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL GIGGLING EXCITEDLY]</font></b>

1562
01:27:20.690 --> 01:27:22.734
- <b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> Eleanor, you did it!
- I know!

1563
01:27:23.985 --> 01:27:25.653
Guys, we need to go.

1564
01:27:26.738 --> 01:27:28.740
<b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> Oh! Yes, yes. Okay. Let's go!

1565
01:27:29.449 --> 01:27:30.533
Wow!

1566
01:27:30.617 --> 01:27:34.245
- Guys, it smells like watermelon.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> This is incredible.

1567
01:27:34.329 --> 01:27:37.332
Eleanor! You made this.

1568
01:27:37.415 --> 01:27:38.625
<b><font color="#cf685c">ELEANOR:</font></b> I did this.

1569
01:27:42.629 --> 01:27:44.672
So, how does it move?

1570
01:27:46.257 --> 01:27:47.258
Right.

1571
01:27:48.176 --> 01:27:49.761
Uh... Oh.

1572
01:27:50.136 --> 01:27:51.137
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CAT MEOWING]</font></b>

1573
01:27:54.057 --> 01:27:55.099
Please don't blow up.

1574
01:27:56.976 --> 01:27:58.394
<b><font color="#ca004b">[MEOWS]</font></b>

1575
01:27:59.938 --> 01:28:01.856
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CAT YOWLS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR GASPS]</font></b>

1576
01:28:02.148 --> 01:28:03.358
<b><font color="#ca004b">[YOWLING]</font></b>

1577
01:28:07.278 --> 01:28:09.531
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL SCREAMING]</font></b>

1578
01:28:15.036 --> 01:28:16.663
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL SCREAM]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[TIRES SCREECHING]</font></b>

1579
01:28:17.080 --> 01:28:18.206
<b><font color="#ca004b">[WOMEN SCREAMING]</font></b>

1580
01:28:27.674 --> 01:28:29.133
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL SHRIEKING]</font></b>

1581
01:28:35.265 --> 01:28:37.058
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHRISTMAS CAROL PLAYING]</font></b>

1582
01:28:47.068 --> 01:28:48.236
There! I see the stage!

1583
01:28:59.289 --> 01:29:00.832
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BARB LAUGHING]</font></b>

1584
01:29:02.750 --> 01:29:05.587
The Charlestown drum majorettes, folks!

1585
01:29:05.670 --> 01:29:09.591
Look at those smiles!
Followed by the...

1586
01:29:15.054 --> 01:29:16.222
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

1587
01:29:17.432 --> 01:29:21.603
The traditional flying watermelon
carriage float, of course.

1588
01:29:22.103 --> 01:29:26.691
What the... Hey! Get this, get this,
get this. You, come on!

1589
01:29:32.363 --> 01:29:33.615
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD GASPING]</font></b>

1590
01:29:37.494 --> 01:29:38.536
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ALL EXCLAIM]</font></b>

1591
01:29:44.918 --> 01:29:48.838
Oh, just a little fun fact.
I played tuba in high school.

1592
01:29:49.839 --> 01:29:52.217
Yeah, it's not a great instrument
for a teenage girl.

1593
01:29:52.300 --> 01:29:56.429
If you blow too hard, you can get
a permanent eye bulge. Just slight...

1594
01:29:56.513 --> 01:29:58.223
Anyway, that's a story for another time.

1595
01:29:58.306 --> 01:30:04.062
Right now, we are headed to the main stage
for the Hamilton High show choir.

1596
01:30:04.145 --> 01:30:05.647
- Sorry.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">WOMAN:</font></b> Ma'am, stop there.

1597
01:30:05.730 --> 01:30:08.983
Actually, she's on stage right now.
She's supposed to sing. Duff!

1598
01:30:09.067 --> 01:30:10.235
Hey, hi.

1599
01:30:11.361 --> 01:30:13.422
- They're with me.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">ANNOUNCER:</font></b> Ladies and gentlemen,

1600
01:30:13.446 --> 01:30:16.407
let's hear it for
the amazing Downtown Crew.

1601
01:30:16.991 --> 01:30:19.327
How fantastic were they?

1602
01:30:22.163 --> 01:30:25.792
You have to make me brave.
I need a spell or something.

1603
01:30:25.875 --> 01:30:28.920
Jane, you know it doesn't work like that.

1604
01:30:29.504 --> 01:30:31.631
I can't change your feelings
with my magic.

1605
01:30:34.008 --> 01:30:35.969
I'm sorry, I can't do this.

1606
01:30:36.386 --> 01:30:37.387
Hey. Listen.

1607
01:30:39.180 --> 01:30:43.518
I didn't believe in you
because I forgot how to believe in myself.

1608
01:30:44.060 --> 01:30:47.146
And I was lost, and I felt scared,

1609
01:30:47.230 --> 01:30:49.774
and I taught you to be scared.

1610
01:30:50.692 --> 01:30:55.280
You don't need a spell
because you are already magical.

1611
01:31:01.244 --> 01:31:02.453
Come on. Let's rush.

1612
01:31:04.539 --> 01:31:06.124
Hey, I'm here. I made it.

1613
01:31:06.583 --> 01:31:10.712
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SIGHS]</font></b> Jane! Thank goodness.
We did not have a Plan B.

1614
01:31:10.795 --> 01:31:11.963
Now get out there.

1615
01:31:12.172 --> 01:31:13.214
Okay.

1616
01:31:14.090 --> 01:31:15.925
You can do this.

1617
01:31:18.011 --> 01:31:21.764
<b><font color="#cf685c">ANNOUNCER:</font></b> I want you to give it up now
for tonight's finale,

1618
01:31:21.848 --> 01:31:27.145
the Hamilton High show choir,
with soloist Jane Walsh!

1619
01:31:44.078 --> 01:31:48.917
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING]</font></b>
You're broken down and tired

1620
01:31:50.585 --> 01:31:51.586
<b><font color="#ca004b">[FEEDBACK OVER MIC]</font></b>

1621
01:31:53.129 --> 01:31:54.130
We...

1622
01:31:56.090 --> 01:31:57.133
In...

1623
01:31:57.217 --> 01:31:58.218
<b><font color="#ca004b">[BREATH TREMBLING]</font></b>

1624
01:31:59.052 --> 01:32:00.220
I'm sorry.

1625
01:32:01.471 --> 01:32:02.555
Oh.

1626
01:32:12.774 --> 01:32:15.527
<b><font color="#ca004b">[WHISPERING]</font></b>
Your dad would be so, so proud.

1627
01:32:15.610 --> 01:32:18.029
Okay? You got this. Yeah?

1628
01:32:18.112 --> 01:32:19.489
<b><font color="#cf685c">CROWD:</font></b> Aw.

1629
01:32:31.000 --> 01:32:33.920
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SINGING]</font></b>
You're broken down and tired

1630
01:32:34.712 --> 01:32:38.007
Of livin' life on a merry-go-round

1631
01:32:38.716 --> 01:32:41.386
And you can't find the fighter

1632
01:32:42.345 --> 01:32:45.682
But I see it in you
So we can walk it out

1633
01:32:45.765 --> 01:32:51.271
Move mountains

1634
01:32:51.354 --> 01:32:52.856
We gonna walk it out

1635
01:32:53.481 --> 01:32:58.528
Move mountains

1636
01:32:59.487 --> 01:33:03.658
And I'll rise up
I'll rise like the day

1637
01:33:03.741 --> 01:33:07.328
I'll rise up
I'll rise unafraid

1638
01:33:07.412 --> 01:33:09.205
I'll rise up

1639
01:33:09.289 --> 01:33:13.585
And I'll do it a thousand times again

1640
01:33:14.711 --> 01:33:18.464
And I'll rise up
High like the waves

1641
01:33:18.548 --> 01:33:22.177
I'll rise up
In spite of the ache

1642
01:33:22.260 --> 01:33:23.428
I'll rise up

1643
01:33:23.970 --> 01:33:28.474
And I'll do it a thousand times again

1644
01:33:28.558 --> 01:33:30.351
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHOIR HUMMING]</font></b>

1645
01:33:30.518 --> 01:33:33.521
When the silence isn't quiet

1646
01:33:34.230 --> 01:33:37.525
And it feels like
It's gettin' hard to breathe

1647
01:33:37.609 --> 01:33:41.029
-And I know you feel like dyin'
-<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHOIR VOCALIZING]</font></b>

1648
01:33:41.654 --> 01:33:44.866
But I promise
We'll take the world to its feet

1649
01:33:44.949 --> 01:33:50.747
And move mountains

1650
01:33:50.830 --> 01:33:52.499
We can walk it out

1651
01:33:52.582 --> 01:33:57.754
Move mountains

1652
01:33:59.422 --> 01:34:02.842
<b><font color="#cf685c">CHORUS:</font></b> Joy to the world

1653
01:34:02.926 --> 01:34:06.221
Joy to the world

1654
01:34:07.180 --> 01:34:12.185
And I will rise a thousand times again

1655
01:34:13.603 --> 01:34:17.315
-For you
-<b><font color="#cf685c">CHOIR:</font></b> Repeat the sounding joy

1656
01:34:17.398 --> 01:34:21.277
-For you
-Repeat the sounding joy

1657
01:34:21.361 --> 01:34:24.447
- For you
- Repeat, repeat

1658
01:34:25.114 --> 01:34:27.742
- For you
- The sounding joy

1659
01:34:29.536 --> 01:34:31.788
-All we need
-Repeat the sounding joy

1660
01:34:31.871 --> 01:34:35.124
-Oh, all we need is hope
-Repeat the sounding joy

1661
01:34:35.208 --> 01:34:38.545
-And for that we have each other
-Repeat

1662
01:34:38.628 --> 01:34:42.799
-And for that we have each other
-Repeat the sounding joy

1663
01:34:42.882 --> 01:34:44.801
We'll rise up

1664
01:34:44.884 --> 01:34:47.387
-Repeat the sounding joy
-<b><font color="#ca004b">[JANE VOCALIZING]</font></b>

1665
01:34:47.470 --> 01:34:50.056
Repeat the sounding joy

1666
01:34:50.849 --> 01:34:54.269
-<b><font color="#cf685c">JANE:</font></b> We'll rise up
-Repeat, repeat

1667
01:34:54.352 --> 01:34:57.355
- For you
- The sounding joy

1668
01:35:00.066 --> 01:35:02.068
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD CHEERING]</font></b>

1669
01:35:15.707 --> 01:35:16.791
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHUCKLES]</font></b>

1670
01:35:18.251 --> 01:35:21.754
She was extremely good!
Oh, my God! Did you see her?

1671
01:35:21.838 --> 01:35:23.256
She did it!

1672
01:35:23.339 --> 01:35:24.507
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHEERING]</font></b>

1673
01:35:24.591 --> 01:35:26.509
- She did it!
- Oh! <b><font color="#ca004b">[GRUNTS]</font></b>

1674
01:35:26.593 --> 01:35:28.678
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCREAMS]</font></b>
What are you doing here?

1675
01:35:28.761 --> 01:35:31.264
I'm here to take you home
before it's too late.

1676
01:35:31.723 --> 01:35:34.017
- No! Hey, quit it!
- Let go of her!

1677
01:35:34.100 --> 01:35:38.396
You're the reason she's in this mess.
She stayed to help a hopeless case,

1678
01:35:38.479 --> 01:35:41.733
and if I don't get her home right now,
she could lose everything. Come with me.

1679
01:35:41.816 --> 01:35:44.485
- Wait. Is that true?
- No! You are not hopeless.

1680
01:35:44.569 --> 01:35:46.613
- Now let go of me! Let go!
- Please. I will not.

1681
01:35:46.696 --> 01:35:50.241
- Let go!
- You cannot take my magic away from me!

1682
01:35:55.371 --> 01:35:58.750
Eleanor Fay Bloomingbottom.

1683
01:36:00.293 --> 01:36:02.462
Don't tell them my middle name.

1684
01:36:02.545 --> 01:36:04.714
You get over here right now!

1685
01:36:05.256 --> 01:36:08.426
This whole mess is
exactly why Fairy Godmothers

1686
01:36:08.510 --> 01:36:10.470
are supposed to follow the rules.

1687
01:36:11.554 --> 01:36:14.807
And you are not a Fairy Godmother.

1688
01:36:14.891 --> 01:36:15.892
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD GASPS]</font></b>

1689
01:36:17.435 --> 01:36:18.895
We're going home.

1690
01:36:20.396 --> 01:36:21.397
Hmph!

1691
01:36:22.774 --> 01:36:23.775
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GASPS]</font></b>

1692
01:36:27.153 --> 01:36:28.404
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD CHEERING]</font></b>

1693
01:36:30.031 --> 01:36:31.032
What?

1694
01:36:31.866 --> 01:36:34.035
I am a Fairy Godmother.

1695
01:36:34.118 --> 01:36:37.455
And what Fairy Godmothers
are supposed to do is help.

1696
01:36:38.331 --> 01:36:41.042
I did. I helped Jane.

1697
01:36:45.004 --> 01:36:47.006
Jane was not the assignment.

1698
01:36:48.049 --> 01:36:52.595
And even if she were,
there are no more assignments.

1699
01:36:52.679 --> 01:36:54.514
Mackenzie was the last one.

1700
01:36:54.597 --> 01:36:57.725
And I do not see a dress or a prince.

1701
01:36:58.184 --> 01:37:01.354
And you did not get her
to happily ever after.

1702
01:37:01.437 --> 01:37:04.482
- But...
- You did not save the Motherland.

1703
01:37:05.108 --> 01:37:07.694
All you did was fail!

1704
01:37:09.988 --> 01:37:11.281
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[MOIRA GASPS]</font></b>
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[ELEANOR GASPS]</font></b>

1705
01:37:11.364 --> 01:37:13.575
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD MURMURING]</font></b>

1706
01:37:13.658 --> 01:37:16.369
- That is not true.
- Excuse me?

1707
01:37:16.452 --> 01:37:19.664
Eleanor, correct me if I'm wrong,
but does your formula require

1708
01:37:19.747 --> 01:37:21.249
my true love to be a prince?

1709
01:37:21.332 --> 01:37:25.128
- Why, no. I guess it doesn't.
- Well, that's good.

1710
01:37:25.211 --> 01:37:27.213
Mia, Jane.

1711
01:37:28.423 --> 01:37:30.383
Then these are my true loves.

1712
01:37:30.800 --> 01:37:32.177
And you didn't fail.

1713
01:37:32.260 --> 01:37:34.596
You helped me remember
how to live happily.

1714
01:37:35.388 --> 01:37:38.600
<b><font color="#ca004b">[SCOFFS]</font></b> That's not the same
as happily ever after.

1715
01:37:38.683 --> 01:37:39.684
Are you sure?

1716
01:37:40.935 --> 01:37:42.353
Four years ago, I...

1717
01:37:43.146 --> 01:37:44.731
I thought my story was over,

1718
01:37:44.814 --> 01:37:47.901
and Eleanor helped show me that it wasn't.

1719
01:37:47.984 --> 01:37:49.110
<b><font color="#cf685c">CROWD:</font></b> Aw!

1720
01:37:49.194 --> 01:37:50.737
That's not how it works.

1721
01:37:50.820 --> 01:37:52.906
Then how it works needs to change.

1722
01:37:53.615 --> 01:37:56.242
We think that love
needs to look a certain way.

1723
01:37:56.659 --> 01:37:59.746
A prince, a castle, a gown.

1724
01:38:00.955 --> 01:38:02.582
We're trapped in the fairy tale

1725
01:38:02.665 --> 01:38:06.628
when the real world
is full of so much more.

1726
01:38:06.711 --> 01:38:09.547
<b><font color="#cf685c">CROWD:</font></b> Aw!
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHEERING]</font></b>

1727
01:38:11.049 --> 01:38:14.302
Instead of telling people
what true love is supposed to look like,

1728
01:38:15.345 --> 01:38:17.180
maybe we should let them tell us.

1729
01:38:18.389 --> 01:38:20.808
Mia, who's your true love?

1730
01:38:21.476 --> 01:38:23.520
- Can I have more than one?
- Sure. Why not?

1731
01:38:23.603 --> 01:38:26.814
Well, Mom and Jane, but also Aunt Paula.

1732
01:38:27.357 --> 01:38:29.317
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD CLAPPING]</font></b>

1733
01:38:29.400 --> 01:38:30.401
<b><font color="#cf685c">PAULA:</font></b> You guys...

1734
01:38:32.987 --> 01:38:36.741
Who's your true love?
And don't just tell me, tell each other.

1735
01:38:36.825 --> 01:38:37.826
You?

1736
01:38:39.369 --> 01:38:40.578
- Us?
- Yes.

1737
01:38:41.287 --> 01:38:43.289
- I love you, Nan.
- <b><font color="#cf685c">CROWD:</font></b> Aw.

1738
01:38:45.792 --> 01:38:46.876
And you.

1739
01:38:49.796 --> 01:38:51.589
<b><font color="#cf685c">BOTH:</font></b> We love you, Jonah.

1740
01:38:52.632 --> 01:38:53.633
Aw.

1741
01:38:54.217 --> 01:38:56.010
Oh! And you, Hugh Prince,

1742
01:38:56.845 --> 01:38:58.221
what does love mean to you?

1743
01:38:58.304 --> 01:38:59.973
Me? Oh, I...

1744
01:39:00.765 --> 01:39:02.976
Right, um... Love?

1745
01:39:03.059 --> 01:39:06.813
Love. Yeah, love.
Love is many, many

1746
01:39:06.896 --> 01:39:08.314
<b><font color="#ca004b">[HESITATES]</font></b>
a splendored thing.

1747
01:39:08.398 --> 01:39:09.482
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD LAUGHS]</font></b>

1748
01:39:09.566 --> 01:39:12.235
No, um, love means...

1749
01:39:13.611 --> 01:39:14.946
I love you, Dad.

1750
01:39:15.446 --> 01:39:18.783
...dressing up as a colonial soldier
'cause you miss your son.

1751
01:39:19.701 --> 01:39:23.746
And sometimes love just means
shoveling someone's driveway.

1752
01:39:27.125 --> 01:39:29.210
That one didn't really make sense.

1753
01:39:30.920 --> 01:39:33.840
Love comes in so many forms, Moira.

1754
01:39:35.258 --> 01:39:36.593
Why can't we see that?

1755
01:39:37.177 --> 01:39:39.846
Eleanor didn't magically fix my life.

1756
01:39:39.929 --> 01:39:42.140
She showed me how to fix it myself.

1757
01:39:44.893 --> 01:39:46.352
That's how we can help them.

1758
01:39:51.441 --> 01:39:53.026
This is a day I thought I'd never see.

1759
01:40:01.201 --> 01:40:03.828
You did well!

1760
01:40:03.912 --> 01:40:05.914
- <b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD CHEERING]</font></b>
- Oh! I did well!

1761
01:40:09.626 --> 01:40:13.129
- Maybe it's time to re-write the book.
- All right.

1762
01:40:13.213 --> 01:40:16.007
Now, let's go home
and save some Fairy Godmothers.

1763
01:40:17.467 --> 01:40:19.385
Thank you for everything.

1764
01:40:21.054 --> 01:40:22.430
Thank you.

1765
01:40:24.140 --> 01:40:26.726
- Go be a Godmother.
- All right.

1766
01:40:40.406 --> 01:40:41.407
Bye!

1767
01:40:48.832 --> 01:40:51.292
<b><font color="#cf685c">MOIRA:</font></b> Wands up!

1768
01:40:53.920 --> 01:40:55.713
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD GASPS]</font></b>

1769
01:40:56.756 --> 01:40:57.966
<b><font color="#ca004b">[PAULA LAUGHS]</font></b>

1770
01:40:58.049 --> 01:40:59.092
<b><font color="#cf685c">MAN:</font></b> What?

1771
01:40:59.300 --> 01:41:00.593
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CROWD CHEERING]</font></b>

1772
01:41:00.677 --> 01:41:02.303
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CHITTERING]</font></b>

1773
01:41:06.266 --> 01:41:07.433
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]</font></b>

1774
01:41:20.321 --> 01:41:21.573
<b><font color="#ca004b">[ELECTRICITY BUZZING]</font></b>

1775
01:41:24.075 --> 01:41:25.952
<b><font color="#cf685c">MACKENZIE:</font></b> Gary!

1776
01:41:29.038 --> 01:41:33.001
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Wait! We're not done yet.

1777
01:41:34.836 --> 01:41:37.797
Good morning, Motherland!

1778
01:41:38.298 --> 01:41:41.509
No, I don't think I'm shouting.
Hold, please.

1779
01:41:42.135 --> 01:41:45.889
Why don't we kick things off
with something a bit more groovy today?

1780
01:41:46.472 --> 01:41:47.473
Take it away.

1781
01:41:49.225 --> 01:41:54.105
Now, I told you this wasn't a fairy tale,
but that was only half true.

1782
01:41:54.606 --> 01:41:57.400
In the end, Eleanor got hers all right.

1783
01:41:57.483 --> 01:42:00.862
Only it wasn't anything like
she'd read in those books.

1784
01:42:00.945 --> 01:42:03.156
And that was a good thing.

1785
01:42:03.239 --> 01:42:06.201
We weren't just old.
We'd become old-fashioned.

1786
01:42:06.826 --> 01:42:09.704
There are those who might say...
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CLEARS THROAT]</font></b>

1787
01:42:09.871 --> 01:42:12.874
I had spent my whole life
believing in fairy tales.

1788
01:42:13.416 --> 01:42:16.419
Well, now I believe in them
more than ever.

1789
01:42:17.295 --> 01:42:20.048
It's just that they come
in all different shapes and sizes.

1790
01:42:20.256 --> 01:42:24.135
Just like us. And thanks to
our newly patented approach

1791
01:42:24.219 --> 01:42:27.764
of, "Forget ever after,
just live happily," we've been busy.

1792
01:42:27.847 --> 01:42:32.477
<b><font color="#cf685c">AGNES:</font></b> Eleanor! Wand up, kid.
We've still got a lotta work to do.

1793
01:42:32.977 --> 01:42:35.230
<b><font color="#ca004b">[CLEARS THROAT]</font></b>
Fairies...

1794
01:42:35.313 --> 01:42:36.856
<b><font color="#ca004b">[POP MUSIC PLAYING]</font></b>

1795
01:42:36.940 --> 01:42:38.233
<b><font color="#ca004b">[GIGGLES]</font></b>
